hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2401","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: 'He has more right to her so long as she is in the bleeding.'"
"2402","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, she said: 'She becomes separated from her husband when she enters the third menstruation.'"
"2403","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: 'When she enters the third menstruation, he is quit of her.'"
"2404","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: 'When the divorced woman menstruates the third time, she is quit of him, except that she may not marry until she becomes pure.'"
"2405","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he used to say: 'When she enters the third menstruation, he has no retraction over her and no inheritance between them.'"
"2406","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Salim ibn 'Abdillah, that he used to say the like of what Zayd said."
"2407","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Ibrahim, that 'Umar and Ibn Mas'ud said: 'He has more right to her so long as she has not bathed after the third menstruation.'"
"2408","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, she said: 'Al-aqra are the periods of purity.'"
"2409","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from one who informed him, from 'A'ishah, the like of that."
"2410","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: 'He has more right to her so long as she has not bathed after the third menstruation.'"
"2411","Chapter: one who says to his wife: 'Observe your waiting period.' Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: 'It used to be said: When he says: ""Observe your waiting period,"" then it is a divorce.'"
"2412","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and 'Ubaydah from Ibrahim, that they both said: 'When a man says to his wife: ""Observe your waiting period,"" while intending divorce, they said: One, and he has more right to her; and if he did not intend divorce then it is nothing.'"
"2413","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurrah informed us, from al-Hasan, that he said: 'When a man says to his wife: ""You are divorced, observe your waiting period,"" then it is one; and when he says: ""You are divorced, and observe your waiting period,"" then they are two.'"
"2414","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Makhul, he said: 'When he says to his wife: ""Observe your waiting period,"" or ""Count your term,"" then it is a divorce and he has more right to her.'"
"2415","Sa'id narrated to us, Fudayl said: From Mansur, from Ibrahim: 'When a man says: ""Observe your waiting period,"" then it is a divorce.'"
"2416","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, regarding a man who said to his wife: 'Observe your waiting period,' he said: 'It is a divorce, and he has more right to her.'"
"2417","Chapter: one who says to his wife: 'You are divorced whenever you wish.' Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, regarding a man who said to his wife: 'You are divorced whenever you wish,' he said: 'She is divorced whenever she wishes.'"
"2418","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, regarding a man who married his slave-girl to a man and gave her a dower, then freed her before her husband consummated with her, and she was given the choice and chose herself, he said: 'They are separated, and the dower is returned to the husband.'"
"2419","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, regarding a man who married his slave-girl for a named dower, then her master freed her before consummation, he said: 'If she chooses herself, the dower is voided.' And if she chooses her husband before consummation, Mughirah said: Ibn Shubrumah said: The dower belongs to the master."
"2420","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: 'If she chooses herself after her husband has consummated with her, then the dower belongs to the master.'"
"2421","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Ubaydillah ibn 'Ubayd al-Kala'i, from Makhul, regarding a slave who married a slave-girl and she was freed before he consummated with her, while he had given her her dower, and she was given the choice and chose herself, he said: 'What he gave her is returned to him.'"
"2422","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Ubaydillah ibn 'Ubayd al-Kala'i, regarding an owned man who married a slave-girl, then she was freed before him: is the slave-girl given the choice to stay with him or is she compelled to him? He said: 'Rather she is given the choice.' I said: And how if she had borne her master a boy, so her husband became her son's slave - does that forbid her to him or not? He said: 'I see that she becomes forbidden to him because of that.' I said: And how if she was with him a short or long while, then he wanted to take back from him - does she have that or not? And she said: 'I did not know that I had any say in my affair.' He said: 'When she settles until he comes to her, then she is his wife.' I said: And how if the slave became hers through her inheritance after her child? He said: 'She is not lawful to him; and 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: He is ordered to divorce her.'"
"2423","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, that he used to say regarding the slave-girl who is freed: she is given the choice over a slave husband and not given the choice over a free husband; then if the slave consummates with her, she has no choice."
"2424","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: 'Regarding the slave-girl when she is freed and has a husband, if he consummates with her before she chooses, then she has no choice.'"
"2425","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: 'If she did not know that she has the choice, then she has the choice, even if her husband had consummated with her.'"
"2426","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say: 'She has the choice when she learns.'"
"2427","Chapter: what has come regarding the choice of the slave-girl. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from a slave-girl of Banu 'Adi ibn Ka'b who was freed while she had a husband; Hafsah said to her: 'I shall inform you, though I would not love for you to do it: you have the choice so long as your husband has not touched you; then when he touches you, you have no choice.' She said: 'Then bear witness that I have parted from him.' Then she parted from him."
"2428","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur and Yunus informed me, from al-Hasan, that he used to say regarding the slave-girl when she is freed and has a free husband: she has no choice; and if he is a slave, then she has the choice."
"2429","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, he said: 'The slave-girl has the choice when she is freed, even if she is under a man of Quraysh.'"
"2430","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: 'She has the choice, whether her husband was a slave or free.' Hushaym said: And this is the position."
"2431","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Shubrumah al-Hamdani informed us, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi say: 'She has the choice, whether her husband was free or a slave.'"
"2432","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that he would not grant her the choice over a free husband."
"2433","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from 'Ata and Nafi', that they both said: 'The husband of Barirah was a slave called Mughith.'"
"2434","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: When Barirah was given the choice, I saw her husband following her in the streets of Madinah, his tears flowing upon his beard; then al-'Abbas spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his behalf, asking him to intercede with her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: 'He is your husband and the father of your child.' She said: 'Do you command me with him, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'I am only an intercessor.' She said: 'Then if you are an intercessor, I have no need of him.' He said: So she chose herself. He was called Mughith, and he was a slave of the family of al-Mughirah of Banu Makhzum. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-'Abbas: 'Do you not marvel at the intensity of Barirah's hatred for her husband and the intensity of her husband's love for her?'"
"2435","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us, from 'Ikrimah, that Ibn 'Abbas said regarding the husband of Barirah, called Mughith, a slave of such-and-such tribe: 'As though I see him now, following her in the streets of Madinah, weeping.'"
"2436","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from 'A'ishah, she said: 'The husband of Barirah was free.'"
"2437","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, she said: The husband of Barirah was free. She said: When she was freed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice, and she chose herself. Her family wanted to sell her while stipulating wala, so that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: 'Buy her, then free her; for wala belongs only to the one who frees.'"
"2438","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, he said: I do not know whether I heard it from the hadith of Ibrahim or another, from 'A'ishah, that she said: 'O Messenger of Allah, people give charity to Barirah and she gifts to us, so may we eat?' He said: 'Yes; indeed it is charity upon her, and it is a gift for you.'"
"2439","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Husayn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: There were three rulings concerning Barirah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted her the choice over her husband; her masters sold her to 'A'ishah while stipulating that wala belongs to them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Wala belongs to the one who frees'; and meat was given to her in charity and she gifted it to 'A'ishah, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and wanted to eat from it, and she said: 'It was given in charity to Barirah.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'It is charity upon Barirah, and a gift for us.'"
"2440","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Wala belongs to the one who frees.'"
"2441","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, regarding the slave-girl under a free man or a slave who is then freed, he said: 'She has the choice when she is freed.'"
"2442","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Alqamah al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar said: 'Any slave-girl under a slave who is freed, she has the choice so long as he has not touched her.'"
"2443","Chapter: a young girl is divorced before reaching menstruation. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughirah from Ibrahim, and Muhammad ibn Salim from al-Sha'bi, that they said regarding a young girl when she is divorced before reaching menstruation: 'She observes her waiting period by months; then if she menstruates a day or two before the three months pass, she restarts the waiting period by menstruation; then if she menstruates a day or two after the months pass, her waiting period has ended.'"
"2444","Chapter: a slave-girl is divorced then freed during the waiting period. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed me, from al-Sha'bi, and 'Ubaydah from Ibrahim, they said: 'When a man divorces his wife while she is a slave-girl with one divorce, then she is freed during the waiting period, her waiting period is that of a free woman and he has retraction over her; and if he divorced her twice then she was freed during the waiting period, her waiting period is that of a slave-girl and he has no retraction over her.'"
"2445","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from a man, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: 'She observes the waiting period of a free woman and he has retraction over her; then when the waiting period ends, if he wishes to propose to her, let him propose.'"
"2446","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Khusayf informed us, from Mujahid, regarding the slave-girl who is divorced then freed while in the waiting period, he said: 'She restarts the waiting period of a free woman if it was from one divorce; and if it was from two divorces then she is separated, observing three courses.'"
"2447","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Amr ibn Aws, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: 'If I could make the waiting period of the slave-girl one and a half menstruations, I would do so.'"
"2448","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Amr ibn Aws, that 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: 'If I could make the waiting period of the slave-girl one and a half menstruations, I would do so.' A man said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, then make it a month and a half.' He said: So he fell silent."
"2449","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Amr ibn Aws mention, from a man of Thaqif, he said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, upon the pulpit say: 'If I could make the waiting period of the slave-girl one and a half menstruations, I would do so.' A man said: 'Then make it a month and a half.' He said: So he fell silent."
"2450","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, that 'Ata used to say: 'The waiting period of the slave-girl who does not menstruate is two months.'"
"2451","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he used to say regarding the waiting period of the slave-girl: 'Can half the punishment be upon her while half the concession is not for her?'"
"2452","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: 'The divorce of the slave-girl is two divorces, and her waiting period is two courses; and if she does not menstruate then a month and a half.'"
"2453","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: 'The divorce of the slave-girl is two divorces, and her waiting period is two menstruations.' He said: 'And when a slave-girl is cleared of the womb, she is cleared by one menstruation.'"
"2454","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of the family of Talhah, say: Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, he said: 'Umar said: 'The slave marries two and divorces twice, and she observes two menstruations; then if she does not menstruate, a month and a half' - or he said: 'two months' - Sufyan doubted. [Flag: the printed text's attribution wavers between the slave's waiting period and the slave-girl's; translated literally.]"
"2455","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from 'Abd al-Karim, from Ibn Sirin, he said: 'Umar said: 'The divorce of the slave-girl is two divorces, and her ila is two months.'"
"2456","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, and Yunus from al-Hasan, and Muhammad ibn Salim from al-Sha'bi, that they said regarding the waiting period of the slave-girl when she is divorced: 'If she menstruates then two menstruations; and if she does not menstruate then a month and a half; and if he died leaving her, then two months and five days.' Hushaym said: And this is the position."
"2457","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Attab narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to us, from Mujahid, he said: 'Every woman observing her waiting period by courses whose menstruation then ceases, she restarts with months; and if she was observing her waiting period by months then menstruates, she restarts with menstruation.'"
"2458","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, regarding a man who marries a young girl before she reaches menstruation then divorces her, he said: 'She observes three months; then if she menstruates before the months end, she restarts with menstruation.'"
"2459","Chapter: what has come regarding the waiting period of umm al-walad. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that he said regarding the waiting period of umm al-walad when her master dies leaving her or frees her, he said: 'The waiting period of a free woman.'"
"2460","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from 'Amir, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: 'When umm al-walad is freed, her waiting period is three menstruations.' Hajjaj said: 'Then if he died leaving her, the like of that.'"
"2461","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: 'The waiting period of umm al-walad is three menstruations.'"
"2462","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Ali and 'Abdullah, they said regarding umm al-walad: 'When her master dies leaving her, they said: She observes three courses.'"
"2463","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: 'The waiting period of umm al-walad is three menstruations.'"
"2464","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, and from one who heard al-Hakam narrate from Ibrahim, he said: 'She observes three menstruations or three months.'"
"2465","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj informed us, from Nafi', that Ibn 'Umar said: 'The waiting period of umm al-walad is one menstruation.'"
"2466","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Umar, he said: ""She observes her waiting period with a single menstruation."""
"2467","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, the same as that."
"2468","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that he said: ""Four months and ten (days)."""
"2469","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, narrating from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, concerning the waiting period of the umm al-walad (a slave woman who bore her master a child) when her master dies leaving her: he said: ""Four months and ten (days)."""
"2470","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from Humayd al-Tawil, that they both heard al-Hasan saying: ""Four months and ten (days)."""
"2471","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur and Abu Hurrah informed us, from al-Hasan, that he said in his final position: ""She observes the waiting period with a single menstruation; but if her master had freed her, then three months."""
"2472","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, that he was asked about that, and he said: ""Among them are those who say: three months, and among them are those who say: four months and ten (days)."""
"2473","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: It was said to him, does the umm al-walad observe a waiting period of four months and ten days when her master dies leaving her? He said: ""Then would you not give her an inheritance?"""
"2474","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi Umayyah, from Ibrahim, he said: ""The private part of a free woman is not cleared (as lawful) with less than three menstruations."""
"2475","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said concerning the slave woman when she is freed: ""She observes a waiting period of three menstruations."""
"2476","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to us, from Ata, he said: ""When a man frees his umm al-walad or a slave girl whom he used to have intercourse with, her waiting period is three menstruations."""
"2477","Chapter: a woman divorced with one or two divorces whose menstruation then stops, then she dies, and her husband inherits from her. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, that Alqamah divorced his wife and she remained sixteen months, or seventeen months, or eighteen months, then died before completing the waiting period; so Alqamah asked Abdullah, who said: ""Allah has returned her inheritance to you."""
"2478","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, that Alqamah divorced his wife with one divorce or two, and she menstruated once or twice, then her menstruation stopped for seventeen months or eighteen months, then she died; so Alqamah came to Abdullah asking him about her inheritance, and he said: ""Allah has kept her inheritance for you,"" so he gave him her inheritance."
"2479","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, that he divorced his wife with one divorce, and she menstruated once or twice in sixteen months or seventeen months, then did not menstruate the third time until she died; so he came to Abdullah and mentioned that to him, and Abdullah said: ""Allah has kept her inheritance for you,"" so he gave him an inheritance from her."
"2480","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed, from al-Sha'bi, and Humayd, from al-Hasan, and Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, that they said: ""If she menstruates, her waiting period is by menstruation, even if she menstruates once every year."""
"2481","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: ""If a woman menstruates once every year, three months suffice her."" And Tawus said: ""Her periods (quru') are whatever they are."""
"2482","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, that Habban ibn Munqidh had under him two wives, a Hashimite woman and an Ansari woman; he divorced the Ansari woman while she was nursing, and she remained a year, then he died leaving her at the turn of the year; so she came to Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: I am due an inheritance. Uthman said: ""This is a matter about which there is no knowledge; go to Ali."" So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""You swear at the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that you did not menstruate three menstruations; if you swear, the inheritance is yours."" So she swore, and Ali made her a partner with the Hashimite woman in the eighth; then Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the Hashimite woman, as though excusing himself to her: ""This is the judgment of your cousin."""
"2483","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he said concerning a man who divorces his wife with one divorce or two, then her menstruation stops and it is not known what stopped it: ""She waits nine months from the time of suspicion; if a pregnancy becomes evident in her, that is it; and if none becomes evident, she waits three months, then marries whomever she wishes."""
"2484","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: ""She waits a year after (the time of) suspicion, then three months after the year, then marries if she wishes."""
"2485","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that Ibn Mas'ud used to say: ""She observes the waiting period by menstruation if she menstruates."""
"2486","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought (the case of) a man who divorced his wife, and she menstruated three menstruations in a month, or in thirty-five nights; so he said to Shurayh: Judge concerning her, O Shurayh. He said: Should I judge while you are present, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: Judge. He said: If she brings evidence from upright women of her intimate family whose truthfulness and justice are approved, testifying that she saw what forbids her prayer, of the menstrual blood that is (true) menstruation, washing from every period and praying, then her waiting period has ended; otherwise she is lying. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, in the Byzantine tongue: ""He is right."" [Flag: the introductory phrase is terse/garbled in the source.]"
"2487","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Shurayh was sitting with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when a woman came disputing with her husband, for he had divorced her and she claimed she had menstruated three menstruations in a month; so Ali said: O Shurayh, judge between them. He said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Commander of the Faithful, should I judge between them while you are sitting? He said: You shall surely judge concerning her. So Shurayh said: If she brings an intimate group of her family whose religion and trustworthiness are approved, testifying that she menstruated three menstruations, washed at every menstruation, and prayed, then it is as she said; otherwise she is lying. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Qalun"" - in the Byzantine tongue - meaning: he spoke the truth."
"2488","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, concerning a woman who was divorced and observed a waiting period of three menstruations in forty nights; Ibrahim said: ""If she brings evidence from upright women testifying that she saw what forbids her prayer, of the menstrual blood that is the known menstruation at every (time of) purity, and she prays, then her term has ended; otherwise she is lying."""
"2489","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Fudayl narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: ""It is part of trustworthiness that a woman is entrusted over her private part."""
"2490","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: ""The woman is entrusted over her private part."""
"2491","Chapter: one who takes back his wife while he is absent and she does not know. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that Abu Kanaf divorced his wife, then travelled, then took his wife back while she did not know; so she observed the waiting period, and when her waiting period ended she married; then he came to Umar and informed him; Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""The negligence came from your side."" Then he wrote for him: if her (new) husband has not consummated with her, he (the first husband) is more entitled to her. So he came while she had prepared and combed herself for her husband to enter upon her, with women with her; so he was alone with her and adjured her by Allah: did he come near you? She said: No. So he closed the door excluding the women, and in the morning he read Umar's letter to them, and he was confirmed (to remain) with his wife."
"2492","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, with this hadith."
"2493","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, that Abu Kanaf divorced his wife while he was absent and informed her of the divorce, then took her back and did not inform her of the return; then Abu Kanaf came, and there she was, married; so he came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and mentioned that to him; Umar said: ""Hasten; if you reach her before he consummates with her, she is your wife; but if you come after he has consummated with her, there is no claim over her."" So he came and found her on her wedding night, and said: Seek permission for me to see her, for I have a need with her. So they did, and he seized her by the leg."
"2494","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, and Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: ""If a man divorces his wife and informs her of her divorce, then takes her back and conceals the return from her until the waiting period ends, there is no claim for him over her."""
"2495","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: ""If a man divorces his wife, then takes her back while absent or present, without informing her of the return until the waiting period ends, there is no claim for him over her."""
"2496","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Attab narrated to us, he said: Khusayf informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said concerning the absent man who writes to his wife with divorce, then writes to her with the return, but it does not reach her until she marries: ""If he reaches her before the other (husband) consummates with her, she is his wife; but if he does not reach her until he has consummated with her, she is separated (from him)."""
"2497","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, and Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: ""If he takes her back during the waiting period, she is his wife, whether she married or did not marry, whether he consummated with her or not, whether she knew or did not know."""
"2498","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that a man divorced his wife with one divorce and informed her of the divorce, then travelled and wrote to her with the return, but the letter did not reach her until the waiting period ended; so he came to Shurayh and mentioned that to him; Shurayh said: ""If she has married, there is no claim for you over her; but if she has not married, raise her to the authority, and they will be the ones who return her to you or withhold you from her. And inform them of the return as you inform them of the divorce."""
"2499","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, and Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, and Abu Ishaq, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, that they said concerning a man who divorces his wife once or twice, then has intercourse with her during the waiting period: ""It is a return, and he bears witness to what he did."""
"2500","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from Ibn Sirin, he said: A man came to Imran ibn Husayn and said: he divorced his wife without calling witnesses, and took her back without calling witnesses. So Imran said to him: ""You divorced outside the (proper) waiting manner, and took back contrary to the Sunnah; bear witness to what you did."""
"2501","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Rawah, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about a man who divorces secretly and takes back secretly, and he said: ""You divorced outside the (proper) waiting manner, and took back in blindness; bear witness to what you did."" [Flag: the word for ""in blindness"" is garbled/uncertain in the source.]"
"2502","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus informed, from al-Hasan, he said: ""If he divorces without calling witnesses, and takes back without calling witnesses, let him bear witness to what he did."""
"2503","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind and Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Return acts of ignorance to the Sunnah."""
"2504","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: ""I disputed with a man of the early reciters concerning a man who divorces his wife and conceals her return from her until her waiting period ends; so I asked Shurayh, and he said: for him is the breaking wind of the hyena (i.e. nothing)."""
"2505","Chapter: divorce is by the men and the waiting period is by the women. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub: he heard Sulayman ibn Yasar saying: ""Nufay', the youth of Umm Salamah, divorced a free woman with two divorces, and they were keen to return her to him, but Uthman and Zayd ibn Thabit refused that."""
"2506","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Ikrimah, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: ""Divorce is by the men and the waiting period is by the women."""
"2507","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: he heard him saying: ""Divorce is by the men and the waiting period is by the women."""
"2508","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: ""The free man divorces the slave woman with three divorces, and she observes a waiting period of two menstruations; and the slave divorces the free woman with two divorces, and she observes a waiting period of three menstruations; so divorce is by the men, and the waiting period is by the women."""
"2509","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Abdullah said: ""The Sunnah is by the women in divorce and the waiting period."""
"2510","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, that they both used to say that."
"2511","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, the same as that."
"2512","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad and al-Hasan, that they both used to say: ""Divorce and the waiting period are by the women."""
"2513","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, he said: ""The slave divorces the free woman thrice, and the free man divorces the slave woman twice."""
"2514","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: ""Divorce and the waiting period are by the women."""
"2515","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from one who said: al-A'mash narrated to us, he said: Abdullah said: ""The Sunnah is by the women in divorce and the waiting period."""
"2516","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, the same as that."
"2517","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Umarah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ali, he said: ""Divorce is by the women and the waiting period is by the women."""
"2518","Chapter: where the woman whose husband has died observes her waiting period. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, that some women of Hamdan whose husbands were killed sent to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud asking him about going out; so he said: ""Go out in the daytime, keeping one another company; but when it is night, do not spend the night away from your houses."""
"2519","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah and al-A'mash informed us, from Ibrahim, that some women of Hamdan whose husbands were killed felt lonely, so they came to Ibn Mas'ud and asked him; one of them (the narrators) said: visit one another in the daytime. And the other said: talk in the daytime as you wish, and return at night to your houses."
"2520","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The husbands of some women died while they were performing Hajj or Umrah, so Umar ibn al-Khattab sent them back from Dhu al-Hulayfah to observe their waiting periods in their houses."
"2521","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, sent back some women who had set out as pilgrims during their waiting periods, returning them from Dhu al-Hulayfah to their houses."
"2522","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that a woman whose husband died while she was in her waiting period, then her father died; Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about her, and he permitted her to spend a night or two nights (away)."
"2523","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: ""The woman whose husband has died does not leave her house except for a right: visiting a sick person, or a relative, or a matter that is unavoidable; and the woman divorced thrice is like that."""
"2524","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: ""The woman whose husband has died does not go out except for a right: visiting a father, or a relative she keeps ties with; and she does not spend the night except in her house."""
"2525","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, from al-Harith, that a man said to Ibn Mas'ud: I divorced my wife, and she set out in the morning going to her family. So Ibn Mas'ud said: ""It would not please me to have her religion for a date or two dates."" [Flag: terse/garbled source; meaning of the date remark is obscure.]"
"2526","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sulaym informed us, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Mas'ud when a man came to him and said: What do you think of a woman who was divorced and in the morning returned to her family? So Abdullah said: ""It would not please me to have her religion for a date."""
"2527","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he moved his daughter Umm Kulthum when Umar was struck (assassinated), moving her during her waiting period."
"2528","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about the woman whose husband has died: does she go out during her waiting period? He said: ""The companions of Abdullah were the strictest about that; they used to say: she does not go out; while the Shaykh - meaning Ali, may Allah be pleased with him - would move her."""
"2529","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ata and Jabir ibn Zayd, concerning the woman whose husband has died, he said: ""She does not go out."""
"2530","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn al-As divorced his wife - she being the daughter of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hakam, the nephew of Marwan - and her father moved her during her waiting period; so A'ishah sent to Marwan: ""Fear Allah and return the woman to her husband's house to observe her waiting period in it."" So Marwan sent back to her: her father has overpowered me in that. Yahya said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to me that Marwan, when A'ishah sent to him, said: Has the hadith of Fatimah bint Qays not reached you? She said: Leave aside the hadith of Fatimah. So Marwan said: Is the evil through you? Sufficient for you is the evil between these two."
"2531","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran narrated to me, from his father, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about the affair of Fatimah bint Qays, why did she move? He said: ""Because she was harsh against them while she was with them in the house, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed her; then he did not leave her to move to her family."" [Flag: source terse; ""did not leave her to move"" rendered literally.]"
"2532","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Salamah, from Fatimah bint Qays, that her husband divorced her in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he used to spend on her a meagre maintenance; when she saw that she said: By Allah, I shall surely speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); if maintenance is due to me, I shall take what suffices me. So she mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""There is no maintenance for you, nor lodging."""
"2533","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated to me, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: My husband divorced me, and I disputed with him over lodging and maintenance before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he decreed lodging and maintenance for me; but when it reached him that he had divorced me thrice: ""He assigned me neither lodging nor maintenance, and I was commanded to observe my waiting period in the house of a (certain) woman""; so it was said to him: people talk to her (visit her). She said: ""So he commanded me to observe my waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."" [Flag: internal tension in the report rendered literally as in source.]"
"2534","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah, Husayn, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, and Dawud, and Mujalid informed me, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays and asked her about the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she said: ""My husband divorced me irrevocably, and I disputed with him before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over lodging and maintenance, but he assigned me neither lodging nor maintenance, and commanded me to observe my waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."" Mujalid said in his hadith: ""O daughter of the family of Qays, lodging and maintenance are only upon one whose return (to her) remains."""
"2535","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking lodging and maintenance, and he said: ""Do you hear, O you woman? Lodging and maintenance are only for one over whom her husband retains the return."""
"2536","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, and Husayn narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that Umar said: ""We do not abandon the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and the Sunnah of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the word of a woman; we do not know, perhaps she forgot or it was confused to her."""
"2537","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: The word of Umar was mentioned to him, so al-Sha'bi said: A woman of Quraysh, of intellect and judgment - would she forget a judgment decreed upon her?"
"2538","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar and Abdullah used to assign lodging and maintenance to the woman divorced thrice. He said: And when the hadith of Fatimah bint Qays was mentioned in Umar's presence - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to observe her waiting period in other than her husband's house - he said: ""We would not permit in our religion the testimony of a (single) woman."" Sa'id said: And the word of Umar is dearer to us than this."
"2539","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say concerning the woman divorced thrice and the woman whose husband has died: ""There is no lodging for her nor maintenance, and they both observe their waiting periods wherever they wish."""
"2540","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to say concerning the woman divorced thrice and the woman whose husband has died: ""They have neither lodging nor maintenance, and they both observe their waiting periods wherever they wish, and they may perform Hajj during their waiting periods if they wish."""
"2541","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, that a woman of the people of Madinah whose husband died, and al-Qasim ibn Muhammad was asked, and he said: She does not leave until her waiting period ends. And Salim ibn Abdullah was asked, and he said the same as that; so they came to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and asked him about that, and he said: ""Let her remain until the waiting period ends, for I hope that if she does, she will marry on the night she becomes lawful."" So she did, and she married on the night she became lawful."
"2542","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his aunt Zaynab, from Furay'ah bint Malik, the sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that her husband went out seeking some hired labourers of his and was killed at the edge of al-Qadum; so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him; she said: And I asked him for the transfer to my brothers. She mentioned some state of her situation. She said: So he permitted me; but when I turned away he called me: ""Remain in your house until the decree reaches its term: four months and ten (days)."""
"2543","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: He was asked about women who were divorced at al-Qanatir and came to al-Kufah; so Ibrahim commanded them to return to where they were divorced, to observe their waiting periods there."
"2544","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus and Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, concerning the woman whose husband has died, he said: ""She may move if she wishes, and wear whatever she wishes."""
"2545","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, he said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and said: ""I divorced my wife thrice, and she refuses to observe her waiting period in her house."" He said: Do not leave her. He said: She refuses but to go out. He said: Restrain her. He said: She has brothers with thick necks (stubborn). He said: Seek the help of the authority against them."
"2546","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: ""A man died while his wife was in a rented house; so Ibrahim was asked: where does she observe her waiting period? He said: I consider it good that she pay the rent and observe her waiting period in the house she was in."""
"2547","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he was asked about a man who divorces his wife while she is in a rented house; he said: ""She stays in it until her waiting period ends, and the rent of the house is upon her husband."""
"2548","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', that Ibn Umar complained (of illness), and a daughter of his whose husband had died came to visit him; when night came she asked his permission to spend the night, so he commanded her to return to her husband's house."
"2549","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, he said: My father said: ""The divorced woman does not move, unless her family migrates, then she migrates with them."""
"2550","Chapter: what has come concerning the maintenance of the pregnant woman. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh, he said: ""Maintenance is spent on the pregnant woman whose husband has died from the whole of the wealth."" He said: And our companions used to say: ""If the wealth is of value, maintenance is spent on her from her share; but if the wealth is little, maintenance is spent on her from the whole of the wealth."""
"2551","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, concerning the woman whose husband has died while she is pregnant, he said: ""For her is maintenance from the whole of the wealth."""
"2552","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, concerning the woman whose husband has died while she is pregnant, he said: ""For her is maintenance from the whole of the wealth."""
"2553","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: ""Yazid ibn Abi Muslim sent to me asking me about the woman whose husband has died while she is pregnant; so I said to him: maintenance is spent on her from the whole of the wealth until she gives birth; then when she gives birth, the inheritance is divided. So Yazid said to me: We divide the inheritance, setting aside for what is in her womb the share of a boy; if she brings a boy, his share is his; and if she brings a girl, she is given her share and the rest divided among the heirs? So I said: What if she brings both, twins? For I and Amrah were born in one belly."""
"2554","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Hashim narrated to us, from Shurayh and Ibrahim, that they both said: ""The maintenance of the pregnant woman whose husband has died is from the whole of the wealth."""
"2555","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: ""Her maintenance is from her share."""
"2556","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hakam and Kathir narrated to me, from Ata, that he said: ""From her share."""
"2557","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: ""The woman whose husband has died has no maintenance of the pregnant woman."" Sa'id said: And this is what is acted upon."
"2558","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say concerning the woman whose husband has died while she is pregnant: ""For her is maintenance from the whole of the wealth until she gives birth."""
"2559","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi and Ibrahim, that they both used to say that."
"2560","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, that he used to say: ""For her is maintenance from the whole of the wealth until she gives birth."""
"2561","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla and Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he used to say: ""For her is maintenance from the whole of the wealth until she delivers what is in her womb."""
"2562","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: ""There is no maintenance for her except from her share."""
"2563","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: One who heard al-Hakam informed me, narrating from Abu Sadiq, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: ""For her is maintenance from the whole of the wealth."""
"2564","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: ""Her maintenance is from her share."""
"2565","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla and Ash'ath informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: ""There is no maintenance for her."""
"2566","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say concerning the woman divorced thrice, the woman who ransoms herself (mukhtali'ah), and the woman whose husband has died while she is pregnant: ""For them are lodging and maintenance until the waiting period ends."""
"2567","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: One who heard al-Hakam informed me, narrating from Ibrahim, the same as that."
"2568","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a woman who learned that her husband died after she had spent his wealth; he said: ""What she spent from the day her husband died is counted, and made from her share."""
"2569","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say concerning the umm al-walad when he dies leaving her while she is pregnant: ""If she bears him alive, her maintenance is from his (the child's) share; but if it is dead, then from the whole of the wealth."""
"2570","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from Ibn Sirin, he said: He used to say: ""Maintenance is spent on her from the whole of the wealth."" He said: That was his opinion, until he took charge of the estate of a nephew of his, who left an umm al-walad of his while she was pregnant; so he disliked acting in her case by his opinion, and sent to Abd al-Malik ibn Ya'la, the judge of al-Basrah, and asked him about that; so he said: There is no maintenance for her."
"2571","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, he said: ""When a man divorces a slave woman while she is pregnant, there is no maintenance for her, because his child belongs to other people."""
"2572","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say: ""If the slave woman is under a free man or a slave, and he divorces her twice while she is pregnant, maintenance and lodging are upon her husband until she delivers her burden."""
"2573","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: ""If he divorces her twice while she is pregnant, maintenance is upon him, whether she is free or a slave, and whether her husband is free or a slave."""
"2574","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to consider maintenance due to a woman upon her husband until he consummates with her."
"2575","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Husam ibn Misak informed us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: ""There is no maintenance for her unless she seeks it."""
"2576","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say: ""She has no maintenance upon her husband if the withholding is from her side."""
"2577","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah and Jarir narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say the same as that."
"2578","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: ""It is decreed for a woman upon her husband in her food half a sa' of wheat every day."""
"2579","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: ""There was allotted to the divorced woman half a sa' every day of wheat."""
"2580","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he decreed for a woman in her food fifteen sa' by the Hajjaji (measure), and two dirhams for her oil and needs every month."
"2581","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Waki' narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: We measured (calibrated) the sa' of Umar and found it to be Hajjaji. Sa'id said: The Hajjaji is the mudd of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2582","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a woman harmed by her husband: ""So al-Sha'bi allotted for her every month fifteen sa' and two dirhams."""
"2583","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who is absent from his wife without sending her maintenance; he said: ""She is fed from her husband's wealth."""
"2584","Chapter: a woman asking her husband for divorce. Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma' - meaning al-Rahabi - from Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""There is no woman who asks her husband for divorce without a matter wronging her, but she will find the fragrance of Paradise (forbidden to her)."" [Flag: the negation verb rendered literally; sense: she shall not find/smell it.]"
"2585","Abu Qudamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Ahwal narrated to us, that a woman came to al-Hasan and said: O Abu Sa'id, her husband is one who fasts much and prays (at night) much, but she does not love him; may she ransom herself from him? He said: No; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Those who pull away and those who seek khul' are the hypocrites (among women)."" She said: Repeat it to me; so he repeated the hadith to her. She said: By Allah, I shall surely be patient. When she left, al-Hasan said: I did not think there remained a woman who restrains herself upon what is disliked for what reached her from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2586","Hazm ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Those who pull away and those who seek khul' are the hypocrites (among women)."""
"2587","Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from al-Haytham ibn Malik, that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of her husband, and he said: ""What do you want? Do you want to marry a young man with flowing abundant hair, upon every lock of which is a devil? Or to seek khul', so that you are with Allah more foul than the carcass of a donkey?"""
"2588","Sharik narrated to us, from Qays ibn Wahb, that a woman ransomed herself from her husband for what she had taken from him, and entered into something of their affair, so Shurayh permitted that."
"2589","Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib or al-Hasan - Hammad doubted - that a daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of her husband; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: ""Return, for I dislike for a woman to trail her skirt complaining of her husband."""
"2590","Hushaym narrated to us: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to consider khul' invalid without the authority."
"2591","Chapter: what has come concerning khul'. Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: ""Khul' is not permitted except before the authority."""
"2592","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: One of our companions informed us, from al-Sha'bi: ""They are upon whatever they agree upon; even if it is without the authority, it is permitted."""
"2593","Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: It was said to him: When a woman wants to ransom herself from her husband, she says: I shall not fulfil an oath for you, nor obey a command of yours, nor wash for you from major impurity. So al-Sha'bi said: The woman acts wickedly, but she does not abandon washing from major impurity. As though he disliked this statement."
"2594","Hushaym narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that a woman said to her husband: I shall not fulfil an oath for you, nor obey a command of yours, nor wash for you from major impurity. So he said with his hand: I shall not do, nor do - whatever woman dislikes her husband, he takes from her and lets her go."
"2595","Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Qays al-Masir, from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: I was sitting with Shurayh when a man and a woman came to him disputing before him; the man kept saying: ""By Allah, were it not for your wealth with me, I would divorce you."" So the woman said: It is yours, on condition you divorce me. He said: You are divorced. She said: Add to me. He said: You are divorced. She said: Add to me. He said: You are divorced. So I said: I see you have only lost - your wife is separated from you and you have paid. Shurayh said: The religion of Allah is then in your hand; they are upon whatever they agreed upon."
"2596","Hushaym narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that a woman said to her husband: I leave for you what of my dower is upon you, on condition you divorce me. He said: Bear witness. She said: Bear witness. He said: So you are divorced. She said: No, by Allah, until you pass them thrice. He said: So you are divorced thrice. She said: You have divorced me, so return my wealth to me. So they disputed before Shurayh; the companions of Shurayh said: We see only that your wife is separated from you, and we see only that you have paid her wealth. So Shurayh said: Do you then see that? They said: Yes. He said: Islam is then narrower than the edge of the sword. Then he said to the man: As for your wife, she is not lawful to you until she marries another husband; and as for your wealth, it is yours."
"2597","Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who says to his wife: I have released you by khul', though he had not released her; he said: She is now released by khul'. And Hammad said: ""There is nothing in her wealth (for him)."""
"2598","Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: ""When a man says to his wife: I have released you by khul', though he had not released her, she is now released by khul', and he has nothing."""
"2599","Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: ""They used to dislike khul'."""
"2600","Hushaym narrated to us: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Shihab al-Khawlani, that a woman purchased her divorce from her husband for a thousand dirhams; so that was raised to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he permitted it, saying: ""This is a woman who bought herself from her husband by purchase."""
"2601","Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said: ""Khul' is what is less than the hair-tie of the head; and a woman may ransom herself with part of her wealth."""
"2602","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: ""He takes from the woman who seeks khul' up to her hair-tie."""
"2603","Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in his taking from her more than he had given her when he releases her by khul'."
"2604","Hushaym narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Jabir ibn Haywah [Flag: source apparatus notes the name is likely corrupted; the correct name is Raja' ibn Haywah], from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, that he saw no harm in his taking from her more than he had given her. He said: And he recites this verse: {There is no blame upon them in what she ransoms herself with}."
"2605","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""He does not take from the woman who seeks khul' more than he had given her."""
"2606","Sufyan narrated to us: A man narrated to me - more than fifty years ago I heard him - narrating from his father, from Ali, he said: ""He does not take from the woman who seeks khul' more than he had given her."""
"2607","Hushaym narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, that Habibah bint Sahl was under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, and there was in his character something (harsh) toward her; so she came in the darkness before dawn and sat at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when the Messenger of Allah came out he said: ""Who is this?"" She said: I am Habibah bint Sahl. She said: Neither I nor Thabit. He said: ""Thabit is indeed praised""? She said: And so he is, but neither I nor he. Nothing happened until Thabit came; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He takes his garden."" She said: Let him take it. And he had given it to her as her dower, so he took his garden, and she stayed with her family."
"2608","Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, she said: Habibah bint Sahl came - a woman of the Ansar, under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas - and said: O Messenger of Allah, neither I nor Thabit, complaining of something of him; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take from her your garden."" So he took from her, and she stayed in her house."
"2609","Hushaym narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Abi Miskin informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, he said: A woman came to Umar ibn al-Khattab having become defiant toward her husband; so he admonished her, reminded her, and commanded her to obey her husband; she said: If you return me to him, I shall surely kill myself. So he commanded her to the stable of beasts, and she remained in it three (days/nights); then he sent to her: How did you find your place where you were? She said: I found no rest since I was with him except in these three nights. So he said to her husband: Release her by khul' for less than the tie of her head; there is no good for you in her."
"2610","Hushaym narrated to us: Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, he said: A woman came to Ali ibn Abi Talib and said: ""Separate me from my husband."" He said: I do not possess that; he gave you his wealth and made you lawful by the Book of Allah. She said: By Allah, you shall surely separate me from him, or I shall kill him. He said: By Allah? She said: By Allah. He said: By Allah? She said: By Allah. He said to her husband: Release her by khul' for less than the tie of her head; there is no good for you in her. Juwaybir said: So I said to al-Dahhak: Does he take from her more than he had given her? He said: Yes, even if she gives him a hundred thousand; she is but a woman who bought herself by purchase."
"2611","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he disliked that a man take from her (in khul') more than what he had given her."
"2612","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik informed us, from 'Ata, that he disliked that he take from her more than what he had given her."
"2613","Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: When the provocation (al-dar') comes from his side, it is not lawful for him to take anything from her; but if it comes from her side, then let him take."
"2614","Hushaym narrated to us, 'Ubaydah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say: When the provocation is from his side, whatever he takes from her is like carrion, blood, and the flesh of swine."
"2615","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Yazid al-Madani, he said: 'Umar said: Grant her khul' even if it be for (the worth of) her earring."
"2616","Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: The ransom (fidyah, khul' compensation) is not lawful until she disobeys him and does not obey him, and causes him to break his oath."
"2617","Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: Khul' is not valid until it originates from the woman's side. And Sufyan said on another occasion: There is no harm in khul' when it comes from the woman's side."
"2618","'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, Khusayf informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, concerning the woman who ransoms herself (al-muftadiyah), he said: I do not think he should take all her wealth; rather let him leave something for her."
"2619","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: When the wife becomes recalcitrant toward her husband, he admonishes her and reminds her; if she returns to what he likes, that is it; if she does not, he boycotts her in bed; if she returns, that is it; if she does not, he strikes her a non-severe beating; if she returns to what he likes, that is it; otherwise it has become lawful for him to take from her and release her."
"2620","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say concerning the mukhtali'ah (the woman divorced by khul'): She has no maintenance unless that is stipulated against her husband."
"2621","Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about the mukhtali'ah, whether she has maintenance, and he said: How can she have maintenance when you take her wealth?"
"2622","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from his companions, that they used to say concerning the pregnant mukhtali'ah: She is entitled to maintenance unless her husband disclaims it."
"2623","Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Jumhan al-Aslami, that Umm Bakr obtained khul' from her husband in the time of 'Uthman, and he said: It is one pronouncement of divorce, unless they had named something (as compensation), in which case it stands as they named."
"2624","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, he said: Jumhan al-Aslami granted his wife khul', then he regretted and she regretted, and they came to 'Uthman ibn 'Affan and mentioned that to him, and he said: It is one pronouncement of divorce, unless you named something, in which case it stands as you named. And my father used to say: Khul' is an irrevocable divorce, she observes 'iddah of three menstrual cycles, and her (former) husband has most right to propose to her during the 'iddah."
"2625","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: When he accepts the ransom, it is one pronouncement of divorce, and he may propose to her during the 'iddah if he wishes and she wishes."
"2626","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say: Whoever accepts wealth in exchange for divorce, the divorce is irrevocable, with no right of return."
"2627","Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from Husayn al-Harithi, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Whoever accepts wealth in exchange for divorce, it is an irrevocable divorce with no right of return."
"2628","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Ibrahim, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that he did not consider any divorce irrevocable except khul' or three (pronouncements)."
"2629","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Talhah, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, the like of that."
"2630","Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he brought back together a man and his wife after two divorces and a khul'."
"2631","Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from 'Ikrimah, he said: Everything (every separation) that wealth permits (i.e., effected for compensation) is not a (revocable) divorce."
"2632","Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, he said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Sa'd ask Ibn 'Abbas about a man who divorced his wife twice and then she obtained khul' from him, and he said: Let him marry her if he wishes; Allah mentioned divorce at the beginning of the verse and at its end, and khul' is in between."
"2633","Khalid narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', from Abu Razin, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I heard Allah say: Divorce is twice, so where is the third? He said: Retaining in kindness or releasing with kindness."
"2634","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', from Abu Razin, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, divorce is twice, so where is the third? He said: Retaining in kindness or releasing with kindness."
"2635","Sa'id narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who took an oath of abstention (ila') from his wife, then four months passed and she obtained khul' from him, then he married her during her 'iddah and divorced her before consummating with her, he said: Ibrahim used to say: She gets the full dower and starts the 'iddah anew; while al-Hasan and 'Amir used to say: She gets half the dower and completes the remainder of her 'iddah. I said to Mansur: Which of the two opinions is dearer to you? He said: The opinion of al-Hasan and 'Amir."
"2636","Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu 'Abdullah al-Shaqari, from Ibrahim, concerning the woman under ila' and the divorced woman: when her husband proposes to her during her 'iddah and then divorces her before consummating with her, she gets the complete dower and the (previous) 'iddah is terminated."
"2637","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: When he marries his wife while she is in the 'iddah of khul' or ila' and divorces her before consummating with her, she gets the full dower and a complete 'iddah."
"2638","Hushaym narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Sabrah al-Hamdani informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said the like of that."
"2639","Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj and Muhammad ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, the like of that."
"2640","Hajjaj narrated to us, from 'Ata, he said: She gets the remainder of the dower and completes the rest of her 'iddah."
"2641","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus and Mansur narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say the same as 'Ata said."
"2642","'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam, they both said: When a man irrevocably divorces his wife after having consummated with her, then marries her during her 'iddah of the divorce and divorces her before consummating with her, she gets the complete dower; but if he marries her after her 'iddah has ended, she gets half the dower."
"2643","'Attab narrated to us, from Khusayf, he said: Maymun ibn Mihran used to say: She gets half the dower, whether he marries her during the 'iddah or after the 'iddah."
"2644","Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me, from Ibn 'Awn al-A'war, from Abu al-Darda', he said: Divorce catches the mukhtali'ah so long as she is in the 'iddah."
"2645","Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from al-'Ala' ibn 'Utbah, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah, attributing the report (to the Prophet), the like of that."
"2646","Sa'id narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah al-Basri, from Ibrahim, he said: Every woman in whose womb is a man's fluid observes 'iddah from him and does not observe 'iddah from another; it is lawful for him to marry her and not lawful for another to marry her, and divorce applies to her."
"2647","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: When he divorces the mukhtali'ah during the 'iddah, the divorce applies to her."
"2648","Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Bayan, from al-Sha'bi, and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: When the mukhtali'ah is divorced during the 'iddah, the divorce is counted against her."
"2649","Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Whoever pronounces divorce during an 'iddah, the divorce applies to her."
"2650","Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: When a woman is observing 'iddah of khul' or ila' and her husband divorces her during the 'iddah, the divorce applies to her."
"2651","Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj and Muhammad ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say: His divorcing her binds her so long as she is in the 'iddah."
"2652","Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, that he used to say: His divorcing her binds her."
"2653","Hushaym narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi 'Abdullah informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, that Ibn Mas'ud used to say: His divorcing her binds her so long as she is in the 'iddah."
"2654","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata, he said: Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn al-Zubayr were asked about divorce after khul', and they did not differ: there is no divorce after khul'."
"2655","Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ikrimah, he said: Divorce after khul' is nothing."
"2656","Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus and Mansur, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: His divorcing her does not catch her when she is in an irrevocable 'iddah."
"2657","Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from 'Ata, that he heard him say the like of that."
"2658","Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Hurmuz, from Jabir ibn Zayd, that he said that (i.e., the same)."
"2659","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, and Malik ibn Mighwal, from al-Sha'bi, that they said: The 'iddah of the mukhtali'ah is like the 'iddah of the divorced woman."
"2660","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who divorces his wife, while she is a slave-girl, twice, and then buys her, they said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband, and she becomes lawful to him only through the same door by which she was forbidden to him."
"2661","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, concerning a man who had a slave-girl with him and divorced her twice and then bought her: may he have intercourse with her? Masruq disliked that."
"2662","Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from 'Ali, and al-Hakam, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. One of the two mentioned, from 'Ubaydah, from 'Ali."
"2663","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: I was told that 'Uthman ibn 'Affan and Zayd ibn Thabit said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"2664","Hushaym narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Hakim al-Ansari informed me, Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to us, that a man married a slave-girl belonging to Kathir ibn al-Salt and divorced her irrevocably, then time passed over whom it passed, and the man acquired wealth, so Kathir ibn al-Salt came and bought the slave-girl from him; when he had concluded (the purchase) for him, he said: Do not hasten until I return to you. Then he went to Marwan ibn al-Hakam and mentioned that to him, and Marwan said to him: Go to Zayd ibn Thabit and ask him about that. The man went to Zayd. Sulayman ibn Yasar said: He came to Zayd while I was with him and asked him, and he said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. Kathir went to the man and informed him, and the man said: Bear witness that he has freed her, married her, and given her such-and-such as dower. Kathir said: Do not hasten until I return to you. He went to Zayd ibn Thabit and mentioned that to him, and he said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"2665","Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Ma'bad, that a slave belonging to Ibn 'Abbas divorced his wife twice, and he said to him: Take her back; but he refused, so he gifted her to him and said: Make her lawful through right-hand possession."
"2666","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Abu Ma'bad, that a boy belonging to Ibn 'Abbas divorced his wife twice, and Ibn 'Abbas said to him: Take her back, may you have no mother, for you have nothing of the matter; but he refused, so he said: She is yours, so take her."
"2667","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he used to say concerning a man who divorces his wife, while she is a slave-girl, twice, and then her master has intercourse with her: Her husband may propose to her if he wishes. Sa'id said: Evil is what he said."
"2668","Khalid al-Hadhdha' informed us, from Marwan al-Asfar, from Abu Rafi', that 'Uthman ibn 'Affan and Zayd ibn Thabit were asked about that and permitted it, while 'Ali was sitting, so he stood up angry, disliking what they said."
"2669","Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu 'Abdullah al-Shaqari, from 'Amir, from Masruq, concerning a man who had a slave-girl under him and divorced her twice, then her master had intercourse with her: does she become lawful for her husband? He said: I heard Allah the Exalted say: Until she marries another husband, and this one is not a husband."
"2670","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi, concerning the slave-girl when she is divorced and her master consummates with her, that she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"2671","Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn 'Awn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I witnessed Qays al-Zayyat ask Masruq, and he permitted him to marry her; then when he turned away, he called him back and said to him: I disavow before you what I said; by Allah, I do not consider her private part becoming lawful except through a (new) husband. And I do not know what he did."
"2672","Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who divorces his wife or dies leaving her, while she has introduced new things into his house: al-Hasan said: Hers is whatever she locked her door upon, except the man's weapon and his mushaf."
"2673","Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, that he said: Whatever was part of the dower is hers, and whatever was not part of the dower is inheritance."
"2674","Hushaym narrated to us, 'Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: Whatever belongs to the man of the kind women do not have the like of is the man's; whatever is of the kind women have that men do not have the like of is the woman's; and whatever is of the kind both men and women have the like of belongs to the survivor of the two."
"2675","Suwayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Nuh al-Madani of the family of Abu Bakrah narrated to me, al-Hadrami, a man he had named, narrated to me, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women's goods belong to women, and men's goods belong to men."
"2676","Suwayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Shubrumah about that, and he said the like of that, and said: Whatever goods are shared by women and men is between them."
"2677","Suwayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us: I asked Ibn Abi Layla and he said the like of that, except that he said: Whatever goods are shared by men and women belongs to the men, whether alive or dead."
"2678","Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibn Shubrumah and Ibn Abi Layla, that they used to say: Whatever belongs to men is the men's, whatever belongs to women is the woman's, and whatever is shared by men and women is the men's."
"2679","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: One who heard al-Hakam and Ibn Ashwa' informed me, they both said: Whatever belongs to men is the men's, whatever belongs to women is the woman's, and whatever belongs to men and women is the woman's. Hushaym said: And this is the opinion."
"2680","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: One who heard Ibn Dhakwan al-Madini and 'Uthman al-Batti informed me, they both say: Whatever belongs to men and women is between them."
"2681","Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Salim informed us, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi say: When the woman enters upon her husband with goods or jewelry and then dies, it is inheritance, even if her family establishes proof that it was a loan with her, unless they had informed her husband of that."
"2682","Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Amir al-Sha'bi, that a woman married off her daughter, and when she wanted to send her to her husband, she gathered jewelry of hers and attested that the jewelry was hers; al-Hajjaj wrote about that to 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, and 'Abd al-Malik wrote: One of them reports that her daughter has wealth, so he marries her on that basis; so whichever woman carries goods from her family's house, it stays with her until she dies, and it is hers. And al-Sha'bi used to hold that view."
"2683","Suwayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Wahb al-Kala'i narrated to us, from Makhul, that 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz permitted the woman (to dispose of) other than a head or two heads without the husband's order. [Flag: the phrase about head or heads is obscure in the source; translated literally.]"
"2684","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from his father, that Subay'ah bint al-Harith recovered from her postpartum bleeding days after her husband's death, and Abu al-Sanabil passed by her and said: You are not lawful until you wait four months and ten days. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Abu al-Sanabil has lied; it is not as he said; you have become lawful, so marry."
"2685","Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak, he said: Subay'ah bint al-Harith delivered after her husband's death by twenty-three or twenty-five (days); when she recovered, she adorned herself for marriage, and that was criticized and objected to; that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If she does so, her term has indeed ended."
"2686","Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that Subay'ah delivered after her husband's death by about twenty nights, and she adorned herself, and Abu al-Sanabil passed by her and said: As if you want to marry. She said: Have I not become lawful? He said: No indeed, until the latter of the two terms passes over you. She came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Abu al-Sanabil has lied; when you find a man you approve of, marry him."
"2687","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from 'Abdullah, similar to that."
"2688","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Mansur ibn Zadhdhan."
"2689","Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla and Dawud narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to that."
"2690","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, he said: 'Abdullah said: Whomever wishes, I will invoke mutual imprecation (li'an) with him that the short Surah al-Nisa' was revealed after (the verse of) four months and ten days."
"2691","Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he used to say: Whomever wishes, I will swear an oath with him that the short Surah al-Nisa' was revealed after the one in al-Baqarah (containing) four months and ten days."
"2692","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Mas'ud said: Whomever wishes, I will contend with him in mutual oath that the short Surah al-Nisa' was revealed after the one in al-Baqarah."
"2693","Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Ibn Mas'ud said: The term of every pregnant woman is to deliver what is in her womb."
"2694","Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, he said: 'Ali used to say: The latter of the two terms."
"2695","Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, he said: I said to 'Amir al-Sha'bi: I cannot believe that 'Ali said: the latter of the two terms. He said: Yes indeed, so believe it as strongly as you ever believed anything."
"2696","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn 'Abbas, concerning the woman whose husband has died: She waits the latter of the two terms."
"2697","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Ali, the like of that."
"2698","Hushaym narrated to us, Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, he said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) differed about it; some of them said: the latter of the two terms. Then Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The term of every pregnant woman is to deliver what is in her womb."
"2699","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, he said: I heard a man of the Ansar narrate to my father, he said: I heard your father say: When she delivers what is in her womb while her husband is (still) on the bier, she has become lawful."
"2700","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that he used to say: When she delivers, she has become lawful. Then a man of the Ansar said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, say: When she delivers what is in her womb while her husband is (still) on the bier, before he is lowered into his pit, her 'iddah has ended."
"2701","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, that both of them disliked that the postpartum woman marry while she is still bleeding."
"2702","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from al-Harith al-'Ukli, that he saw no harm in her marrying while she is bleeding; he said: But her husband should not consummate with her until she bathes."
"2703","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, and 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, they heard Abu Hurayrah say: I asked 'Umar about a man of the people of al-Bahrayn who divorced his wife twice and her 'iddah ended, then a man married her and divorced her, and she returned to him. He said: She remains on what is left of the divorce."
"2704","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: She remains on what is left of the divorce."
"2705","Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from al-Hasan, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Zayd ibn Thabit, and 'Imran ibn Husayn said: She remains on what is left of the divorce."
"2706","Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, he said: I heard Mazidah ibn Jabir narrate from his father, from 'Ali, the like of that."
"2707","Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Hakam, from 'Abidah, that he used to say: She remains on what is left; his consummating with her does not demolish what has passed of the divorce."
"2708","Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, that Ziyad asked 'Imran ibn Husayn about a man who divorced his wife twice, then her 'iddah ended and she married a man, then he divorced her, then she married the first one. He said: She is with him on one (remaining pronouncement); two have passed and one remains. And he asked Shurayh, and he said: A new divorce and a new marriage. Ziyad said: Shurayh has spoken, and Abu Nujayd has judged."
"2709","Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Amir al-Sha'bi, that Ziyad asked 'Imran ibn Husayn and he said: She remains on what is left. And he asked Shurayh, and he said: The latter consummation demolishes the first divorce. And 'Amir used to take the opinion of Shurayh."
"2710","Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, he said: A new marriage and a new divorce. Dawud said: And 'Amir used to hold it."
"2711","Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: She is with him on three (i.e., with a full fresh count of three)."
"2712","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: She is with him on three."
"2713","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Shurayh, he said: She is with him on three."
"2714","Hushaym narrated to us, from some of his companions, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: A new marriage and a new divorce."
"2715","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Fudayl, from Ibrahim, Mughirah said: And I think I heard it from Ibrahim, that he used to say: When she marries a husband and he consummates with her, his consummation demolishes the remainder of the divorce; but if he does not consummate with her, she remains on what is left."
"2716","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: The companions of 'Abdullah used to say: Marriage demolishes three (prior pronouncements), but does not demolish one and two."
"2717","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who divorces his wife thrice and then denies it, he said: She takes him to the ruler, who makes him swear an oath."
"2718","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he said the like of that; he said: If he swears, then let her ransom herself from him."
"2719","Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Jabir ibn Zayd, that he said: They are two adulterers so long as they stay together."
"2720","Hushaym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a man who divorced his wife thrice and kept coming to her; witnesses testified against him that he had divorced her, and he had been coming to her after the divorce, but he denied their testimony. Al-Sha'bi said: The hadd punishment is averted from him, meaning by his denial, but he is separated from his wife."
"2721","Hushaym narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik informed us, from 'Ata, that he was asked about a man who swore by the divorce of his wife that he had paid her a dirham, while she said: You paid me nothing. He said: He is believed, and the word is his."
"2722","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Kufi informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a man who swore to a man demanding money from him that the sun would not set before he paid him his money, and if he did not, his wife would be thrice divorced; the sun set, and his creditor claimed he had paid him nothing, while his wife said: You have divorced me. He said: He is taken at his word concerning his wife, and his proof against his creditor is that he paid him his due; otherwise he remains liable for his money until he pays it to him. Hushaym said: And this is the opinion."
"2723","Sharik ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Ibn Wabarah, from Ibrahim, that a man was demanding from a man thirteen dirhams, or ten dirhams, or thereabouts, and he said: If I do not bring it, his wife is thrice divorced; then he brought it, but in it was a counterfeit dirham and a bad one. Ibrahim said: Order your wife to observe 'iddah."
"2724","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned that (divorce, i.e., revoked it) until he divorced her while she was pure."
"2725","Hushaym narrated to us, 'Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: That menstrual period is not counted."
"2726","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: If he divorces her once, he has most right to take her back and it (that period) is not counted; but if he divorces her with an irrevocable divorce, she counts it."
"2727","Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that Ibn 'Umar divorced his wife once while she was menstruating, and 'Umar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Order him to take her back and wait with her for purity. Ibn 'Umar took her back, having no need of her. I said to Ibn 'Umar: Did you count that pronouncement? He said: Pshaw! What do you think, if I had been incapable and foolish?"
"2728","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from Ibn Sirin, similar to what Khalid mentioned, except that one of the two claimed that the one who asked him, Did you count that pronouncement, was Yunus ibn Jubayr."
"2729","Hushaym narrated to us, Layth informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that a man came to Shurayh and said: He divorced his wife thrice while she was menstruating. Shurayh said: Have you mixed the lawful with the unlawful and the foul with the good? Leave her until she becomes pure, then begins another menstruation, then she is not lawful, meaning for you, until she marries another husband."
"2730","Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Malik, from Ibn 'Umar, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and 'Umar went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: 'Abdullah divorced his wife while she was menstruating. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is nothing."
"2731","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man divorces his wife while she is pure, she observes 'iddah of three menstrual cycles besides the menstruation from which she became pure."
"2732","Sa'id narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated the two mutual imprecators (li'an) and attached the child to its mother."
"2733","Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separate the two mutual imprecators when I was fifteen years old, and he (the husband) said: O Messenger of Allah, I have lied against her if I take her back."
"2734","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Dinar, he heard Ibn Jubayr say: Ibn 'Umar informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the two mutual imprecators: Your reckoning is upon Allah, and one of you is lying; there is no way for you to her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my wealth? He said: You have no (claim to) wealth: if you told the truth about her, it is for what you made lawful of her private part, and if you lied about her, that is even further from you."
"2735","Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: When they two performed li'an, it (the dower) became binding on him (the husband); he said to her (i.e., demanded): My wealth? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you were truthful, it is for what you made lawful of her private part; if you were lying, it is even further from you. Allah knows that one of you is lying, your reckoning is upon Allah, and there is no way for you to her."
"2736","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn 'Umar about the two mutual imprecators, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated the two brothers of Banu al-'Ajlan (i.e., the man and his wife) and said: Allah knows that one of you is lying, so is either of you repentant? He said that three times."
"2737","Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave one of Banu al-'Ajlan the dower."
"2738","Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Bayan, from 'Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: The mula'anah (the woman subjected to li'an) is graver than stoning."
"2739","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The two mutual imprecators are separated and never come together again."
"2740","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: The slanderer of the son of the mula'anah is flogged, and the mula'anah never marries the mula'in again."
"2741","Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed li'an between a man and his wife; the woman's husband said: By Allah, I have not approached her since we watered after drought; al-'afr is watering the palms after leaving off watering for two months. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make clear. The woman's husband was blond-haired, thin in the legs and arms, and she gave birth to a black curly-haired boy, thick in the arms. Shaddad ibn al-Had said to Ibn 'Abbas: Is she the woman about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I stoned her without proof I would have stoned her? He said: No; that was a woman who had openly committed indecency in Islam. Another man called out to him: O Abu al-'Abbas, what was the boy's description? He said: She bore him with the bad description."
"2742","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Qasim, he said: Ibn 'Abbas mentioned the two mutual imprecators, and 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had said: Is she the one about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I stoned a woman without proof I would have stoned her? He said: No; that woman had openly committed (indecency)."
"2743","Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Massan, from 'Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: The child of the mula'anah is attached to its mother, and if a person slanders him or slanders his mother, he is flogged."
"2744","Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: The child of the mula'anah is attached to its mother, and they (her kin) bear his blood-money for him."
"2745","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Whoever slanders the child of the mula'anah by (mention of) his mother is flogged."
"2746","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Hibban al-Azdi, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Umar, that he said concerning a man who divorces his wife and then slanders her during the 'iddah: If he had divorced her thrice, he is flogged, the child is attached to him, and there is no li'an; but if he divorced her once, he performs li'an with her. Ibn 'Abbas said: If he divorces her thrice and then slanders her in the 'iddah, he performs li'an with her. Jabir ibn Zayd said: The opinion of Ibn 'Umar is dearer to us than what Ibn 'Abbas said."
"2747","Hushaym narrated to us, Harun al-Sulami informed us, from 'Amr ibn Hurmuz, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas, the like of that."
"2748","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: He performs li'an with her when he divorces her thrice and then slanders her during the 'iddah."
"2749","Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who slanders his wife and then divorces her thrice, he said: He does not perform li'an."
"2750","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: When he divorces her with an irrevocable divorce and then slanders her during the 'iddah, he performs li'an with her."
"2751","Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a man who divorces his wife thrice and then slanders her during the 'iddah, he said: He performs li'an with her so long as she is in the 'iddah; once the 'iddah ends, he is flogged and does not perform li'an."
"2752","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: When a man slanders his wife and divorces her thrice, he performs li'an, whether she is pregnant or not; but when he divorces her thrice and then slanders her during the 'iddah, if she is pregnant he performs li'an with her, and if there is no pregnancy he is flogged."
"2753","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: There is no li'an for one who has no right of return."
"2754","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a man who divorces his wife thrice and she gives birth to a child, which he disavows, he said: He performs li'an with her. Al-Harith al-'Ukli said to him: O Abu 'Amr, while Allah says in His Book: And those who accuse their wives, do you consider her his wife when he has divorced her thrice? Al-Sha'bi said: I would be ashamed, when I see the truth, not to return to it."
"2755","Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a man who slanders his wife and then she obtains khul' from him, he said: If she seizes him for the slander, whatever he does not disavow of himself, he is flogged, and what he took from her remains his; but if he performs li'an with her, he returns to her what he took from her."
"2756","Hushaym narrated to us: Mughira informed us, from al-Harith al-Ukli, concerning a man who accused his wife of adultery and then she obtained khul' from him. He said: She has fled from li'an, so there is neither hadd nor li'an; but if he divorces her after accusing her, then he has fled from li'an, so the hadd is inflicted upon him, and there is no li'an."
"2757","Hushaym narrated to us: Uthman al-Batti narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who accused his wife of something from before he married her. He said: He is flogged, and he performs li'an, and she remains his wife."
"2758","Abu Awana narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, concerning four who testified against a woman for adultery, one of them being her husband. He said: The hadd is carried out upon her."
"2759","Hushaym narrated to us: al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi. He said: If they are four, they have protected their backs from the hadd, and the hadd is carried out upon her. Al-Shaybani said: And Hammad informed me, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: The husband performs li'an, and the other three are flogged."
"2760","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning four who testified against a woman for adultery, one of them being her husband. He said: The husband performs li'an and the other three are flogged. Abu al-Zinad said: And this is the view of the people of our city, and it is the adopted saying."
"2761","Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Ma'mar informed me, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib. He said: Li'an is a separating divorce; if he accuses himself of lying, he is flogged, and he may propose to her if he wishes."
"2762","Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib. He said: If the husband who performed li'an accuses himself of lying on the spot, he is flogged and his wife is returned to him."
"2763","Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us: Khusayf informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. He said: When a man performs li'an with his wife, if he accuses himself of lying while she is in her waiting period, he is flogged, and he may marry her if he wishes; but if he does not accuse himself of lying until her waiting period ends, he may never marry her."
"2764","Attab narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Hammad. He said: Whenever he accuses himself of lying, during the waiting period or after it, he may marry her if he wishes."
"2765","Attab narrated to us, from Khusayf, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who marries a woman while she is in another land and then accuses her though he has never seen her. He said: He is flogged and there is no li'an between them; and he mentioned that the blind man is in the same position, as is everyone whose testimony is not accepted. Khusayf said: Hammad said: Every outlet that Allah has granted the husband applies whether he has seen her or not seen her, the two perform li'an; and the blind man and one whose testimony is not accepted are likewise, and the apostate is likewise."
"2766","Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who divorced his wife before consummating marriage with her, then she bore a child and he disowned it. He said: He performs li'an with her, and she is entitled to half the dower."
"2767","Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us: Khusayf informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, concerning a man who accuses his wife and then dies before performing li'an with her. He said: He is held in suspense: if he accuses himself of lying, the hadd is inflicted and he inherits; if he brings witnesses, he inherits; but if he invokes the curse, he is not granted inheritance."
"2768","Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Mughira, from Amir al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who accused his wife and then she died. He said: If he accuses himself of lying, he is flogged and he inherits from her; but if he performs li'an with her, he is cleared of flogging and of inheritance. [Flag: opening of report garbled in print; rendered literally.]"
"2769","Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who accuses his wife but the two do not bring the case forward, that they remain upon their marriage: Nothing separates them except that he performs li'an with her."
"2770","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Bashir narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi. He said: He was asked about a man who accused his wife while she was deaf and mute. Al-Sha'bi said: She neither hears nor speaks, so she can neither confirm him nor belie him; there is neither hadd nor li'an between them."
"2771","Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who accuses his wife while she is in her waiting period. He said: He performs li'an with her so long as he retains the right to take her back."
"2772","Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed me, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who accuses his wife and testifies that she is his sister through breastfeeding. He said: They are separated, she is entitled to the dower, and there is no li'an between them."
"2773","Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd al-Kala'i, from Makhul, that he was asked about a man who divorced his wife twice and then accused her: If he accuses himself of lying, the hadd is upon him, and he may take her back if he wishes; but if he does not accuse himself of lying, he performs li'an with her, they are separated, and they shall never come together again."
"2774","Chapter on a man who says to his wife: I have gifted you to your family. Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurra and Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan. He said: If he gifts her to her family and they accept her, it is three divorces; but if they return her, it is one, and he has more right to her."
"2775","Hushaym narrated to us: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: If they accept her, it is one separating divorce; but if they return her, it is one revocable divorce, and he has more right to her."
"2776","Hushaym narrated to us: Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abd Allah. He said: If they accept her, it is one, and he has more right to her; but if they return her, it is nothing."
"2777","Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim. He said: It used to be said concerning the woman gifted to her family: it is one divorce. Mansur said: It reached me from Ibn Mas'ud that he used to say: If they accept her, it is one, and if they do not accept her, it is nothing."
"2778","Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd al-Kala'i, from Makhul. He said: If they accept her, it is one divorce, and he has more right to her; but if they do not accept her, it is nothing."
"2779","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, the same as that."
"2780","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who says to his wife: I have gifted you to your family. He said: They used to say: it is one divorce, and he did not know whether separating or with right of return."
"2781","Chapter on divorce in which there is no return. Sa'id narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Habib informed me, from Ata, from Ibn Mahak, from Abu Hurayra. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, their seriousness is seriousness and their jest is seriousness: divorce, marriage, and taking back."
"2782","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu al-Darda. He said: Three things are not to be played with; play with them and seriousness are the same: divorce, marriage, and emancipation."
"2783","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu al-Darda. He said: Three things are not to be played with: divorce, emancipation, and marriage."
"2784","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abida al-Salmani. He said: Two things, play with them and seriousness are the same: divorce and marriage."
"2785","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam. He said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib; he said: I heard Marwan ibn al-Hakam say upon this pulpit: Four things, there is no return in them except fulfillment: emancipation, divorce, marriage, and vows."
"2786","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Maysara al-San'ani narrated to us: Muslim ibn Abi Maryam said, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib. He said: Marwan said upon the pulpit of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Four things, there is no turning back in them except fulfillment: divorce, emancipation, marriage, and vows."
"2787","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Sulayman Suhaym, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib. He said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Four things are binding when spoken: divorce, emancipation, marriage, and vows; and four people enter the evening while Allah is displeased with them and enter the morning while Allah is angry with them: men who imitate women, women who imitate men, one who approaches a beast, and one who does the deed of the people of Lut."
"2788","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Suhaym, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar. He said: Four people, Allah Almighty enters the evening displeased with them and enters the morning angry with them: men who imitate women, women who imitate men, one who approaches a beast, and one who does the deed of the people of Lut. And Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Four things are binding upon everyone: emancipation, divorce, vows, and marriage."
"2789","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Alqama al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Amr informed us, he said: Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad entered upon al-Nasri, the governor of Medina, and said: This orphan of yours has sworn by divorce and emancipation. Al-Qasim said: As for divorce, it is up to him; and as for emancipation, it is up to me."
"2790","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Alqama narrated to us, he said: Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Bukayr ibn Muhammad. He said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote: Whatever I have permitted of anything, do not permit the foolish regarding divorce."
"2791","Chapter on a man who puts his wife's affair in her hand. Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Masruq. He said: A man came to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: I put my wife's affair in her hand, and she divorced herself thrice. Umar said to Abd Allah: What do you see? He said: I see it as one, and he has more right to her. Umar said: And I see the same."
"2792","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, concerning a man who says to his wife: Your affair is in your hand, and she divorces herself thrice. He said: Umar and Abd Allah agreed that it is one, and he has more right to her."
"2793","Sa'id narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abu al-Halal al-Ataki. He said: I asked Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him: Commander of the Believers, a man put his wife's affair in her hand? He said: Then her affair is in her hand."
"2794","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abu Rabi'a ibn Abi al-Halal al-Ataki, from his father, that Uthman ibn Affan said concerning 'your affair is in your hand': The judgment is whatever she decrees."
"2795","Sa'id narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, concerning a man who put his wife's affair in her hand, and she returned the affair to him. He said: It is nothing; the judgment is whatever she decreed."
"2796","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he used to say: The judgment is whatever she decreed."
"2797","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he used to say: The judgment is whatever she decreed."
"2798","Sa'id narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar. He said: If a man puts his wife's affair in her hand and she divorces herself once, it is one; or twice, then two; or thrice, then three; unless he disputes with her and says: I only put the affair to you regarding one, and he swears to that; but if she returns the affair, it is nothing; and he used to say: The judgment is whatever she decreed."
"2799","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and others, from Zayd ibn Thabit. He said: If a man gives his wife the choice and she divorces herself thrice, it is one."
"2800","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: When a man gives his wife the choice and he says nothing until they separate, her silence is contentment with her husband; she has no choice whenever she wishes."
"2801","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Kufi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, that both of them said the same as that."
"2802","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd. He said: If a man says to his wife: Your affair is in your hand, it is whatever she says in her sitting; but if they separate, it is nothing; he may not walk in the market while his wife's divorce is in another's hand."
"2803","Sa'id narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, that Ibn Mas'ud said concerning 'your affair is in your hand': If she rises from her sitting, she has no choice."
"2804","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Ash'ath informed us, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir. He said: If she rises from her sitting before choosing, she has no choice."
"2805","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, that he used to say: If a man gives his wife the choice and she chooses her husband, it is nothing; but if she chooses herself, it is one and he has more right to her."
"2806","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd al-Kala'i, from Makhul. He said: If a man puts his wife's affair in her hand and she delays that, she has nothing. [Flag: verb garbled in print; rendered literally.]"
"2807","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, the same as that."
"2808","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that a man wrote to his wife giving her the choice, and she placed the letter under the bed and said nothing. He said: Then she has no choice."
"2809","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from al-Sha'bi. He said: If a man gives his wife the choice three times and she chooses once, it is three; but if he gives her the choice once and she chooses three, it is one."
"2810","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that he said the same as that."
"2811","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Bayan, from Amir al-Sha'bi, and Mughira, from Ibrahim and Amir. They both said concerning a man who said to his wife: Choose, choose, choose, and she chose once. They said: It is three; but if he said to her: Choose, and she chose three, it is one."
"2812","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim. He said: If a man puts his wife's affair in another's hand and he divorces her thrice, it is one, and he has more right to her."
"2813","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a man puts his wife's affair in another's hand, the judgment is whatever he decrees; if he returns her, it is one, and he has more right to her."
"2814","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid. He said: Ibn Mas'ud said: If a man puts his wife's affair in a man's hand and the man rises before decreeing anything in that, he has no authority."
"2815","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who put his wife's affair in the hands of two men and one of them divorced. He said: No, until both gather together."
"2816","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ubayda informed us, from Ibrahim, the same as that."
"2817","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, that a woman said to her husband: If what is in your hand of my affair were in my hand, I would leave you. He said to her: Then your affair is in your hand. She said: You are divorced thrice. That was raised to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he became angry at that, and said: You deliberately take a matter Allah put in your hands and put it in their hands. Then he said: One, and you have more right to take her back."
"2818","Sa'id narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, that a woman said to her husband: If what is in your hand were in my hand, you would know what I do. He said: Then what is in my hand of your affair is in your hand. She said: I have divorced you thrice. They came to Ibn Mas'ud and asked him, and Abd Allah said: May Allah deal with men; they deliberately took something Allah put in their hands and entrusted it to others; it is one; and I shall ask the Commander of the Believers. He asked him, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Dust in her mouth, three times. Then he said to Ibn Mas'ud: What did you say in it? He said: I said: One. He said: Is that your view? He said: Yes. He said: And likewise is my view; had you seen otherwise, you would not have been right."
"2819","Sa'id narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar. He said: Ibn Abbas said: May Allah confound her course."
"2820","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that he was asked about a man who put his wife's affair in her hand and she said: You are divorced, you are divorced. Ibn Abbas said: May Allah confound her course."
"2821","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim. He said: The saying of Ibn Abbas was mentioned before him, and he said: They are the same."
"2822","Sa'id narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Ibrahim. He said: The matter of choice was mentioned before A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice and we chose him, and that was not counted as divorce."
"2823","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abi al-Duha, from Masruq, from A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice and we chose him, and he did not count it as divorce."
"2824","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Muslim, from Masruq, that A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice and we chose him, and he did not count anything against us."
"2825","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, from A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice and we chose him, and it was not divorce."
"2826","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Bayan, from Amir. He said: Abd al-Hamid asked me about choice, and I said: Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud used to say: If she chooses herself, one; but if she chooses her husband, nothing. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: If she chooses her husband, one, and he has more right to her; but if she chooses herself, one separating. And Zayd ibn Thabit said: If she chooses herself, three. He said: Then judge in it by the saying of Abd Allah."
"2827","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, that Umar and Ibn Mas'ud said concerning a man when he gives his wife the choice and she chooses herself: it is one and he has more right to her; but if she chooses her husband, nothing."
"2828","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: If she chooses herself, one separating; but if she chooses her husband, one and he has more right to her."
"2829","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he used to say: If she chooses herself, three; but if she chooses her husband, one. [Flag: an extra word in print marked as scribal error; omitted.]"
"2830","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Zayd ibn Thabit, the same as that."
"2831","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he said: If she chooses herself, three; but if she chooses her husband, one and he has more right to her."
"2832","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: 'Your affair is in your hand' and 'choose' are the same: if she chooses herself, one and he has more right to her; but if she chooses her husband, nothing."
"2833","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, that he used to say that also."
"2834","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Hakam, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: If he puts the affair in her hand, it is in her hand; whatever she decrees is valid."
"2835","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus and Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a man puts his wife's affair in her hand, she is separated by three."
"2836","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abi Ja'far, that he was asked about the woman given choice. He said: If she chooses her husband, nothing."
"2837","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that a man left his family while finding nothing amiss with them, then he found his wife ..... She said: If what is in your hand of my affair were in my hand, you would know how I act. The man said: Yes, yes. They raised it to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari and informed him of their story, and Abu Musa said: That is upon you, that is upon you. [Flag: source text has ellipsis; rendered literally.]"
"2838","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Waki' narrated to us, from al-Hazhāz ibn Mayzan, that Adi ibn Faras gave his wife the choice thrice, each time she chose him, and it was raised to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he separated between them. Sa'id said: Faras is the grandfather of Waki'."
"2839","Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abi Ja'far, that Ibn Abi Atiq put his wife's affair in her hand, and she divorced herself many divorces, and he asked Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: It is one and he has more right to her."
"2840","Sa'id narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she married a daughter of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr called Qurayba to al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr. Abd al-Rahman came from his absence, was displeased at that, and said: Is one like me bypassed regarding his daughters? A'isha said: Do you dislike al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr? We shall put her affair in his hand. Al-Mundhir put the daughter of Abd al-Rahman's affair in his hand, but Abd al-Rahman said nothing in that, and they did not regard that as anything."
"2841","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir. He said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad was asked about a man who said to his wife: Your affair is in your hand, and she said: I am forbidden to you three times. He said: It is one divorce."
"2842","Chapter on albatta, albariyya, alkhaliyya, and alharam. Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that a man was on the side of Urwa ibn al-Mughira, and said to his wife: If you go to the family of al-Mughira, you are divorced irrevocably. The man went until he entered upon Urwa ibn al-Mughira, and Urwa said: Welcome Abu so-and-so, you have come to us, and Umm Bakr, meaning his wife, has come to us. He said: He has divorced her irrevocably, so give me a fatwa. Urwa sent asking about that; Abd Allah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had informed him from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he made it one; and Riyash al-Ta'i informed him that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: It is three. Urwa sent to Shurayh asking him about that, and Shurayh said: As for his saying 'divorced,' she is divorced by the Sunna; but as for his saying 'irrevocably,' it is an innovation; we hold him at his innovation: if he wishes he may advance, and if he wishes he may hold back."
"2843","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Sha'bi, similar to the hadith of Sayyar and Isma'il. He said: When he sent him to Shurayh asking him about that, Shurayh said: Allah Almighty laid down ways, and the servants introduced innovations, and they deliberately mixed their innovations with Allah's ways; so when you are asked about anything of that, distinguish the ways from the innovations, then carry out the ways upon their course, and leave the innovations to their people. As for his saying 'divorced,' she is divorced; but as for his saying 'irrevocably,' it is an innovation; we hold him at his innovation: if he wishes let him advance, and if he wishes let him hold back."
"2844","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, that Umar said: It is one, and he has more right to her."
"2845","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Ja'far, from al-Muttalib ibn Hantab, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him concerning divorce with 'albatta': Keep your wife; one that severs."
"2846","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said that."
"2847","Sa'id narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab made 'albatta' one, and he has more right to her."
"2848","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: 'Albatta' is one, and he has more right to her."
"2849","Sa'id narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Ali, that Rukana ibn Abd Yazid divorced his wife with 'albatta,' and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: What did you intend? He said: One. He said: By Allah, did you intend only one? He said: By Allah, I intended only one. He said: It is one. [Flag: chain name disputed in print collation; rendered literally.]"
"2850","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri was asked about 'albatta.' He said: 'Albatta' with us is the severest of divorce."
"2851","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz asked him about a man who divorced his wife with 'albatta.' He said: Aban ibn Uthman used to make it one, and he has more right to her. Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: Had divorce been a thousand divorces, it would reach that when he says 'albatta.'"
"2852","Sa'id narrated to us: Attab narrated to us, he said: Khusayf informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib. He said: 'Albatta' is three."
"2853","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Mughira, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Umar, concerning a man who said to his wife: You are divorced irrevocably. He said: It is one, and he has more right to her."
"2854","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who said to his wife: You are divorced irrevocably. He said: His intention counts: once, twice, or thrice."
"2855","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who said to his wife: You are free of me. He said: His intention counts."
"2856","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say concerning 'alharam,' 'albatta,' 'alkhaliyya,' and 'albariyya': three, three."
"2857","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he said concerning 'alkhaliyya,' 'albariyya,' and 'albatta': three, three."
"2858","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, he said: As for my memory from al-Hasan, that he said concerning 'alkhaliyya': three. And Hafs ibn Sulayman claimed that al-Hasan said: It is one, and he has more right to her."
"2859","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurra and Ash'ath informed us, from al-Hasan, that he said concerning 'alkhaliyya': one, and he has more right to her."
"2860","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid and Mutarrif narrated to us, that they both heard al-Sha'bi say: People claim that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said concerning 'alharam': it is three, but it is not so; I know what he said better than those who reported that from him; he only said: I neither forbid her nor permit her; if you wish, advance, and if you wish, hold back."
"2861","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr informed us, from Yusuf al-Makki. He said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: He made his wife forbidden upon himself. He said: She is not forbidden upon you. The bedouin said: Does not Allah Almighty say in His Book: 'All food was lawful to the Children of Israel except what Israel forbade himself'? Ibn Abbas laughed and said: What tells you what Israel forbade himself? Then he turned to the people narrating to them, and said: Israel suffered sciatica and it emaciated him, so he vowed to Allah Almighty that if He healed him, he would not eat a vein; that is why the Jews remove the veins from meat."
"2862","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say concerning a man who forbade his wife to himself: It is nothing."
"2863","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who said: What is lawful is forbidden upon me. He said: Upon him is expiation of an oath, so long as he did not intend his wife."
"2864","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say concerning a man who made all lawful forbidden upon himself: It is an oath, unless he intends his wife."
"2865","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from one who narrated to him, from Ibrahim, that he said the same as that."
"2866","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, that he said: If a man says: All lawful is forbidden upon me, it is an oath he expiates."
"2867","Sa'id narrated to us: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Ubayd al-Mukattib. He said: A cow was slaughtered in the quarter, and a man said: What is lawful is forbidden upon me if I eat of it. Ibrahim was asked, and he said: Were it not for his wife, I would command him to eat."
"2868","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ubayd al-Mukattib. He said: Ibrahim was asked, and he said: Were it not for your wife, I would command you to eat of its meat."
"2869","Sa'id narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughira, from Hammad, from Ibrahim. He said: If he intended divorce, otherwise it is nothing."
"2870","Sa'id narrated to us: Qurayr narrated to us, from Isa ibn Umar al-Fariqi al-Hizami, from Amr ibn Murra, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, concerning one who said: What is lawful is forbidden upon me: it is an oath among oaths; he expiates it. [Flag: narrator name uncertain in print; rendered literally.]"
"2871","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Mas'ud. He said concerning 'alharam': it is an oath."
"2872","Sa'id narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ja'far, from his father, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said concerning one who forbids his wife to himself: She is divorced thrice."
"2873","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, that Abu Bakr, Umar, and Ibn Mas'ud said concerning 'alharam': it is an oath."
"2874","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from al-Awwam, from Yusayr ibn Amr. He said: If you refer the report to another, you are sufficed."
"2875","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Some of our companions informed us, from Qatada, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say concerning 'alharam': it is three."
"2876","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath informed us, from al-Hakam, that Ibn Mas'ud used to say concerning 'alharam': If he intended divorce, she is divorced; but if he intended an oath, it is an oath."
"2877","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that he said: If a man says to his wife: You are forbidden upon me, then if he intended three, three; if he intended one, one separating; and if he intended nothing, it is an oath he expiates."
"2878","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim. He said: The least they used to say concerning 'alharam': one separating divorce."
"2879","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Ikrima, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said concerning 'alharam': it is an oath."
"2880","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi. He said: Masruq said: I do not care whether my wife becomes forbidden upon me, or a bowl of tharid becomes forbidden."
"2881","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a man who said to his wife: You are divorced one and a half divorces. He said: They are two divorces."
"2882","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas. He said concerning 'alharam': it is an oath."
"2883","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Ubayda, from Ibrahim, that both of them said concerning a man who said to his slave-girl: She is forbidden upon me. They said: It is an oath he expiates."
"2884","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq. He said: He may have intercourse with her and nothing is upon him."
"2885","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ubayda informed us, from Ibrahim, and Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, that Hafsa, Mother of the Believers, visited her father one day, and it was her day. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and did not see her in the house, he sent for his slave-girl Mariya the Copt and had relations with her in Hafsa's house. Hafsa came upon that state and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you do this in my house and on my day? He said: She is forbidden upon me, and do not inform anyone of that. She went to A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, and informed her of that. So Allah Almighty sent down: 'O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you' up to His saying: 'and the righteous of the believers.' So he was commanded to expiate his oath and to take back his slave-girl."
"2886","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore to Hafsa that he would not approach his slave-girl; he said: She is forbidden upon me. So the expiation for his oath was revealed, and he was commanded not to forbid what Allah made lawful for him."
"2887","Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida, from his father, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, with this hadith."
"2888","Chapter on divorce of minors and what applies in it. Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim. He said: They used to conceal marriage from minors, and they disliked casting divorce upon their mouths."
"2889","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim. He said: They used to conceal marriage from minors for fear of divorce. Mughira said: And Ibrahim feared nothing from a boy except divorce."
"2890","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim. He said: A minor's gift is not valid, nor emancipation, until he reaches puberty; and a girl until she menstruates. And he feared nothing in a minor's matter except divorce."
"2891","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: The divorce of a boy who has not reached puberty is not valid until he reaches puberty."
"2892","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, the same as that."
"2893","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Some of our companions informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib. He said: If he prays, fasts Ramadan, and is intelligent, his divorce is valid."
"2894","Sa'id narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muslim, from al-Sha'bi. He said: The divorce of a minor is not valid."
"2895","Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: The charity of a boy is not valid, nor his gift, nor his divorce, nor his emancipation."
"2896","Sa'id narrated to us: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Khusayf informed us, from Mujahid. He said: If he unlawfully has relations with a woman, it is not lawful for him to marry her mother."
"2897","Chapter on a man who commits adultery with a woman: may he marry her or marry her mother. Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Some of our companions informed us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, concerning a man who committed adultery with his wife's mother. He said: He has violated two sanctities; the unlawful does not forbid the lawful."
"2898","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, that he was asked about that. He said: He separates from his wife and does not remain with her. And he commanded them to go to al-Sha'bi; they went to al-Sha'bi and asked him, and he said the same as what Ibrahim said."
"2899","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far al-Ansari informed us, that a man of Quraysh asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about that, and he said to him: Go to Urwa and ask him, then return to me and inform me what he says to you. He asked Urwa, who said: The unlawful does not forbid the lawful. He returned to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and informed him, and Sa'id said: Urwa spoke the truth; the saying is what he said."
"2900","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning a man who committed adultery with his wife's sister. He said: His wife does not become forbidden to him; he keeps away from her until the other's waiting period ends, then he returns to his wife, seeks forgiveness from his Lord, and does not return."
"2901","1723 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say that."
"2902","1724 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say that."
"2903","1725 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, and Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: If he did that with his wife's sister through breastfeeding, then likewise also."
"2904","1726 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: If a man commits adultery with his wife's mother, his wife becomes forbidden to him."
"2905","Chapter on a man who has two slave women who are sisters and has intercourse with them. 1727 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, that Ibn Umar was asked about a man who has two slave women, and they are sisters, and he had intercourse with one of them and wanted to have intercourse with the other, and he said: That is not allowed for him. It was said: What if he approaches her? He said: No, not until the one he had intercourse with leaves his ownership."
"2906","1728 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, the like of that."
"2907","1729 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sharik ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari and Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: He had two owned slave women who were sisters, and he had intercourse with one of them, then he wanted to have intercourse with the other, so he removed her (the first) from his ownership."
"2908","1730 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say about a man who has intercourse with his (own) slave woman, or another person's slave woman, while she is the sister of his wife through breastfeeding, he said: He is to keep away from his wife until he establishes that the womb of the slave woman is clear."
"2909","1731 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, the like of it."
"2910","1732 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Alqamah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Abd Allah ibn Utbah was sitting in the mosque - or he said: in the gathering - and he called a man, who came until he sat before him, and he spoke to him about something I did not understand. When he stood up he raised his voice, and I thought he wanted me to hear him, and he said: If you wish I would confess; will you not listen to what he says: I have declared one of the two forbidden. They kept pressing Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud until they angered him, and he said: Your camel is part of what your right hand possesses. Then I asked some of them, and they claimed that he (the man) had two owned sisters with whom he had intercourse. [Flag: the phrase about the camel is obscure in the source]"
"2911","1733 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from his father, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about combining a mother and her daughter (in marriage/intercourse), he said: I would not like to permit both of them together. My father said: I kept asking, and (found) Umar was stricter about that than this. [Flag: last clause wording unclear]"
"2912","1734 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from a man, that he had two slave women, a woman and her daughter, and both bore him children, and he asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about that, and he said: Two verses: one of them forbids her to you, and the other permits to you what your right hand possesses, but I would not do it, neither I nor my family."
"2913","1735 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The statement of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was mentioned before Ibn Abbas: one verse permitted them both and one verse forbade them both. Ibn Abbas said: One verse permitted them both and another forbade them both; only my (own) kinship to them forbids (a woman) to me, and the kinship of some of them to others does not forbid (her) to me."
"2914","1736 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah, that a man asked A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, saying to her: A qinnah (a slave born into slavery) has grown old - a slave woman of his with whom he used to have intercourse - and she has a daughter; is it lawful for me to approach her (the daughter)? She said: I forbid you from her, and (so will) whoever obeys me. Sa'id said: And I asked Sufyan about the hadith of Mutarrif, from Ammar, he said, he said: What is forbidden from among slave women is what is forbidden from among free women, except for the number. Mutarrif said: from Abu so-and-so. I said to him: From Abu al-Jahm, from Abu al-Akhdar, from Ammar? He said: Yes."
"2915","1737 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi, from his uncle, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: What is forbidden from among slave women is what is forbidden from among free women, except for the number."
"2916","1738 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ibn Abbas was asked about two sisters from among those whom the right hand possesses, and he said: I neither permit them both nor forbid them both; one verse permitted them both and another forbade them both. This reached Ibn Mas'ud, and he said: Do not combine them both."
"2917","1739 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Bajali, from Qays ibn Abi Asim, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: May a man approach a slave woman and her daughter when both are owned by him? He said: One verse forbade them both and another verse permitted them both, but I would not do it. [Flag: narrator names uncertain in source collation]"
"2918","Chapter on a man who has four wives and divorces one of them. 1740 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, that he asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about a man who has four wives and divorces one, he said: He is not to marry (a new one) until the waiting period of the divorced woman ends."
"2919","1741 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Khusayf informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: He is not to marry until the waiting period of the one he divorced ends."
"2920","1742 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: He is not to marry a fifth (woman) until the waiting period of the one he divorced ends."
"2921","1743 - Sa'id narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, about a man who has four wives and divorces one of them, he said: He is not to marry a fourth (i.e. replacement wife) until the waiting period of the one he divorced ends; but if he had four wives and one of them died, he may marry in her place if he wishes, for death is not like divorce."
"2922","1744 - Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, he said: If he divorced her with three divorces, then let him marry (a new wife immediately)."
"2923","1745 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a man divorces his wife then wants to marry her sister, then if his (divorced) wife is pregnant he is not to marry her sister until her waiting period ends, and if she is not pregnant he may marry her sister if he wishes."
"2924","1746 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: He is not to marry her until the waiting period of her sister ends."
"2925","1747 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he said: If he divorced her with an irrevocable divorce, then let him marry her sister if he wishes during her waiting period."
"2926","1748 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik came to Madinah while intending Hajj, and he wanted to marry (a woman) there while he had four wives, so he asked Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Divorce one of your wives with an irrevocable divorce, then marry. So he did that."
"2927","1749 - Sa'id narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, he said: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik had four wives, and he divorced one definitively and married (a new wife) before she became lawful (i.e. before her waiting period ended), and many of the jurists criticized him for that, but not all of them criticized him. 1750 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: If Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib criticized him, what remains?"
"2928","1751 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: A woman came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Her husband was absent from her and prolonged his absence, so he ordered her to wait four years, and she did. Then she came to him, and he ordered her guardian to divorce her, and he divorced her, and he ordered her to observe a waiting period of three menstrual cycles, and she did. Then she came to him, and he ordered her to observe a waiting period of four months and ten days, and she did, then he ordered her to marry."
"2929","Chapter on the ruling regarding the wife of a missing man. 1752 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar, that he said: The wife of a missing man is to wait four years, then observe the waiting period of a woman whose husband has died, and marry if she wishes."
"2930","1753 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, the like of that."
"2931","1754 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, that a man was snatched away by the jinn in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he remained as long as Allah willed him to remain. Then his wife came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he ordered her to wait four years. When he did not come, he ordered her guardian to divorce her, then he ordered her to observe a waiting period. When her waiting period ended and her husband came, he was given the choice between her and the dower."
"2932","1755 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, that a man of the Ansar went out at night and the jinn snatched him away, and his absence was long. His wife came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: Her husband had been absent from her and his absence was long, so he ordered her to wait four years, and she did. Then she came to him, and he ordered her to marry, and she did. Then her first husband came and went to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and told him, and Umar became angry and said: One of you deliberately stays away long from his family and then does not inform them. He said: Do not hasten against me, O Commander of the Faithful; I went out from my house in the evening and the jinn detained me, and I remained among them as long as Allah willed. Then Muslim jinn raided them and said to me: What are you? I told them, and they said to me: Would you like to return to your land? I said: Yes, so they sent me back; in the night (I travel) as men whom I know, and in the day as a whirlwind that carries me. He said: Then Umar gave him the choice between his wife and the dower, and he chose his wife, so he separated them and returned her to him. Then Umar said: What was their food? He said: Beans, and that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned. He said: And what was their drink? He said: Al-jadaf, meaning that which is not covered."
"2933","1756 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Amr ibn Harim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar, that they both said: The wife of a missing man is to wait four years. Ibn Umar said: She is to be maintained during the four years from her husband's wealth, because she has kept herself for him. And Ibn Abbas said: If that burdens the heirs, then let her borrow; if her husband comes she takes from his wealth, and if he remains absent she repays from her share of the inheritance. And they both said: She is to be maintained after the four years for four months and ten days from the whole of the wealth."
"2934","1757 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abbad, from Ali, about the wife of a missing man, he said: She is his wife."
"2935","1758 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, he said: Ali said: If a woman loses her husband, she is not to marry until his affair becomes clear."
"2936","1759 - Sa'id narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, the like of it."
"2937","1760 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, about a woman to whom her husband's death is reported, or the enemy captures him, he said: She is to wait patiently until she knows his affair with certainty; she is only a woman who has been afflicted."
"2938","1761 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Sayyar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say about the wife of a missing man: If the first (husband) comes, she is his wife and he has no choice; and Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say that. Hushaym said: And it is the (adopted) opinion."
"2939","1762 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid and al-Shaybani narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that he said about the wife of a missing man: If she marries and becomes pregnant by her (second) husband, then it reaches her that the first is alive, he said: She is to be separated from the latter; or (if) her first husband has died, she observes a waiting period from this latter one for the remainder of her pregnancy, and when she delivers she observes a waiting period from the first of four months and ten days, and she inherits from him."
"2940","Chapter on what has come regarding the provision (mut'ah) of the divorced woman. 1763 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that al-Hasan ibn Ali divorced a wife of his and sent to her ten thousand as a provision for her, and she said: A small provision from a beloved one who parts. His statement reached him, and he took her back."
"2941","1764 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, that al-Aswad ibn Yazid divorced his wife and gave her a provision of three hundred dirhams."
"2942","1765 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, that he divorced his wife and gave her a provision of three hundred dirhams."
"2943","1766 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us: al-A'mash informed us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, the like of that."
"2944","1767 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, that Anas ibn Malik divorced his wife and gave her a provision of three hundred dirhams."
"2945","1768 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from his grandfather Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that he divorced his wife and gave her as provision a black slave girl, conferring tahmim upon her."
"2946","1769 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from his mother, that she said: It is as if I am looking at a black slave girl whom Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf gave as tahmim to his wife Umm Abi Salamah when he divorced her during his illness."
"2947","1770 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: The Arabs call the (divorce) provision tahmim."
"2948","1771 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Shurayh divorced a wife called Kubayshah, and gave her a provision which he (the narrator) did not name, and he concealed her divorce from her until her waiting period ended. When he told her, she ordered her clothes to be moved and went out, and Shurayh said: For that reason I concealed it from her; I disliked that she should disobey Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"2949","1772 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us, he said: And Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Shurayh divorced his wife and gave her a provision of five hundred dirhams."
"2950","1773 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Every divorced woman has a provision, except the one he divorces before consummating with her while he had fixed (a dower) for her, for she has half the dower."
"2951","1774 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: Every divorced woman has a provision."
"2952","1775 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, that he said: Every divorced woman has a provision, except the one he divorces before consummating with her while he had fixed (a dower) for her, for she has half the dower."
"2953","1776 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he said about the provision: A shirt, a headscarf, a wrap, and an outer cloak."
"2954","1777 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, and Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, that they both said: Every divorced woman has a provision, except the one he divorces while he had fixed (a dower) for her before consummating with her, for she has half the dower."
"2955","1778 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he was asked about the provision, and he said: Among them was one who gave as provision a servant and maintenance, and one below that gave as provision maintenance and clothing, and one below that gave as provision a wrap, a shirt, and an outer cloak, and one below that gave as provision a single garment."
"2956","1779 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur, Yunus, and Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh, that a woman disputed with her husband before Shurayh about the provision, and Shurayh said: Do not refuse to be among the doers of good; do not refuse to be among the God-fearing. And he did not compel him."
"2957","1780 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, that he said: Every divorced woman has a provision, even the woman who ransoms herself (mukhtali'ah)."
"2958","1781 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn Umar divorced a wife of his, and she said to him: Have you seen anything in me that you dislike? He said: No. She said: Then why is a chaste Muslim woman divorced? He said: So he took her back."
"2959","1782 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: If the matter is delegated to the man and he divorces before touching and fixing (a dower), then she has nothing but the provision."
"2960","1783 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Abi Najih, who was asked about a man who divorces his wife before consummating with her while he had fixed (a dower) for her - does she have a provision? He said: Ata used to say: She has no provision."
"2961","1784 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr saying: Every divorced woman has a provision."
"2962","Chapter on a man whose slave woman bears him children and then he buys her. 1785 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus and Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, about a man who was married to a slave woman and she bore him children, then he bought her, he said: She is a mother of a child (umm walad) and he is not to sell her."
"2963","1786 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: She is a mother of a child."
"2964","1787 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: She is not a mother of a child until she bears another child in his possession."
"2965","1788 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from his companions, from Ibrahim, the like of it. Hushaym said: And it is the (adopted) opinion."
"2966","1789 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Fudayl Abu Mu'adh informed us, from Abu Hariz, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated to us, that a man had a free wife and a slave woman whom he had married, and he had children by her, and each child born to him of the slave woman was set free. He bought her after that and died before she bore him (a child while owned by him). Her children disputed the children of the free woman before Shurayh, and Shurayh sent them to Abidah, and Abidah said: She is a slave woman; she would be freed only if she had borne free children, but she bore them while they were owned, so she is a slave woman. So they freed her from the share of her children."
"2967","Chapter on one who did not consider the divorce of polytheism (i.e. effected before Islam) to be anything. 1790 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he did not consider the divorce of polytheism to be anything."
"2968","1791 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he considered it valid. [Flag: isnad omits Sa'id in source]"
"2969","1792 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us ... al-Sha'bi, that he considered it valid. [Flag: isnad truncated in source]"
"2970","1793 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: Whoever, while upon other than Islam, marries a woman and her daughter, and consummates with one of the two, then they (all) embrace Islam, both have become forbidden to him."
"2971","Chapter on one who divorces his wife thinking he has a right of return. 1794 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from Hammad, about a man who divorces his wife before consummating with her, then thinks he has a right of return over her and has intercourse with her, he said: Upon him is a dower and a half."
"2972","1795 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus and Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he said: A single dower."
"2973","1796 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, the like of the statement of al-Hasan."
"2974","1797 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Hakam, the like of that. Sa'id said: The (adopted) opinion is the opinion of Hammad."
"2975","Chapter on one who sets a time for divorce. 1798 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: Whoever sets a time for divorce, then when that time comes the divorce takes effect."
"2976","1799 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: If he sets a time in divorce and manumission it takes effect, and if he does not set a time it does not take effect."
"2977","1800 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, the like of it."
"2978","1801 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: If a man says to his wife: You are divorced (effective) in a year, then she is divorced at once."
"2979","1802 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he did not defer (the effect) in divorce."
"2980","1803 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur and Yunus, from al-Hasan, that he did not defer (the effect) in divorce."
"2981","Chapter on what has come regarding one who begins with the oath in divorce and manumission before the exception. 1804 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: Shurayh used to say: Whenever one begins with the oath in divorce and manumission before the exception (mathnawiyyah), the divorce and manumission have taken effect upon him."
"2982","1805 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr said: If he does not break (his oath), nothing befalls him."
"2983","1806 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh, he said: If a man begins with divorce it takes effect, whether he breaks (his oath) or not. He said: And Ibrahim used to say: And what does Shurayh know."
"2984","1807 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh, he said: Whoever begins with divorce has no exception."
"2985","1808 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Husayn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, that he used to say: Whoever begins with divorce, the divorce binds him."
"2986","1809 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh, that he used to say: If a man begins with divorce, his condition avails nothing."
"2987","1810 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, about a man to whom his wife said: It has reached me that you have married, and he said: Every wife of mine other than you is divorced. Then he informed him of the statement of Shurayh about advancing the divorce and delaying it. [Flag: report outcome not stated in source]"
"2988","1811 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Sayyar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, he said: Shurayh has indeed left in the hearts of the scrupulous a lingering doubt about it."
"2989","1812 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, about a man who says: If I do not do such-and-such, then his wife is divorced, if Allah wills, he said: His exception counts in divorce and manumission."
"2990","1813 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Ata, Tawus, Mujahid, al-Nakha'i, and al-Zuhri, that they said: If a man says to his wife: You are divorced if you do not do such-and-such, if Allah wills, and she does not do it, then he has his exception."
"2991","1814 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that he considered the exception in divorce to be permissible."
"2992","1815 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, about a man who says to his slave boy: I free you, if Allah wills - he did not consider it a manumission."
"2993","1816 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Hassan informed us, he said: I asked Abu Mijlaz about a man who says: If I enter the house of so-and-so, then his wife is divorced thrice; I said: Except if Allah wills, unless Allah wills. Abu Mijlaz said: Has he not made an exception, so let him enter it if he wills."
"2994","1817 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to allow the exception in divorce, whether he puts the divorce first or last, as long as he joins that with his utterance and speech."
"2995","1818 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Salim informed us, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi saying that."
"2996","1819 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: There is no exception in divorce and manumission."
"2997","Chapter on what has come regarding zihar. 1820 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: Whoever performs zihar from his wife and then divorces her, then another man marries her, then parts from her, and her first husband marries her, he said: He is not to approach her until he expiates."
"2998","1821 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he did not set a time limit in zihar."
"2999","1822 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he did not set a time limit in zihar, except that he says: If I approach you while you are to me like my mother's back; if he says that and four months pass before he touches her, she is separated by ila'."
"3000","1823 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, he said: If a man performs zihar from his wife, the expiation is upon him, whether he fulfills (his oath) or breaks it. [Flag: last clause terse in source]"
